 1767371047.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, we begin by looking closely at artwork—as
 king what we see\, think\, feel\, and wonder. Together\, we'll explore wha
 t we think the artist is trying to say and what the social significance of
  their message might be. Then we'll use our imaginations to respond to any
  aspect of our experience. Poets\, story-tellers\, and essayists are all w
 elcome in this group!Read more about The Photographic Reflex: The Lee Mark
 s and John C. DePrez Jr. Collection (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/exhibit
 ions/2026-08-29-photographic-reflex-marks-deprez.html)  &#160\;  What to B
 ringyour favorite pencil (no pens).  a notebook or paper. Clipboards are a
 vailable to borrow.  a phone or camera to take a picture of the art for la
 ter reference.    &#160\;Know Before You GoArrive early\, check in\, and g
 et ready for an on-time start.Readwhere to find us\, where to park\, acces
 sibility\, and museum guidelines.About Your Facilitator  Dedaimia Whitney 
 earned an MFA in fiction from Indiana University under the direction of Sc
 ott Russell Sanders. She taught creative writing at Franklin College for m
 any years. She has served the museum as a docent since 2019. Her favorite 
 works of art are those that are both visually stimulating and thought-prov
 oking.
