LAST-MODIFIED:20260708T153854Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2258144-writing-in-the-galleries
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  In this workshop\, we begin by looking c
 losely at artwork—asking what we see\, think\, feel\, and wonder. Togeth
 er\, we'll explore what we think the artist is trying to say and what the 
 social significance of their message might be. Then we'll use our imaginat
 ions to respond to any aspect of our experience. Poets\, story-tellers\, a
 nd essayists are all welcome in this group!</p><p><a href="https://artmuse
 um.indiana.edu/exhibitions/2026-08-29-photographic-reflex-marks-deprez.htm
 l">Read more about The Photographic Reflex: The Lee Marks and John C. DePr
 ez Jr. Collection</a></p><p>  &#160\;</p><h3>  What to Bring</h3><ul><li>y
 our favorite pencil (no pens).  </li><li>a notebook or paper. Clipboards a
 re available to borrow.  </li><li>a phone or camera to take a picture of t
 he art for later reference.  </li></ul><p>  &#160\;</p><h3><strong><span d
 ata-contrast="none">Know Before You Go</span></strong></h3><ul><li data-le
 veltext="" data-font="Symbol" data-listid="2" data-list-defn-props="{&q
 uot\;335552541&quot\;:1\,&quot\;335559683&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335559684&quot\
