X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 130": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2345843-public-tour-nature-inspired-art"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_130
SUMMARY:Public Tour: Nature-inspired Art
DTSTART:20260906T173000Z
DTEND:20260906T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260709T122811Z
UID:20260906T173000Z-2347065@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260906T173000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,512,640/26850_bamboo_basket_by_tanabe_kochikusai.rev.1750
 250115.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences
DESCRIPTION:The tour visits three floors of the museum\, looking at a vari
 ety of nature-inspired artworks from global cultures\, including nature-in
 spired photography in the featured exhibition The Photographic Reflex: The
  Lee Marks and John C. DePrez Jr. Collection (https://artmuseum.indiana.ed
 u/exhibitions/2026-08-29-photographic-reflex-marks-deprez.html).  This tou
 r changes each time\, based on what's on view. Additional tour highlights 
 may include:from the forest of Papa New Guinea\, an artwork made from natu
 ral materials\, representing a leaf spirit\, worn for a night dance  a tre
 asured bowl that held kola nuts\, for welcoming guests to an African palac
 e  a sacred object from an indigenous culture (Maori)\, made for ocean voy
 ages from a single tree that can live to be 1\,000 years old  a large guar
 d\, with ancient origins\, finely crafted\, by a Kenyan artist\, into an e
 xquisite food storage container and later repaired  Hand-crafted bamboo ba
 skets from Japan  Paintings of larkspurs\, chrysanthemums\, and more    Pl
 us\, look for signs of nature and discuss the influence of garden experien
 ces on I.M. Pei's iconic architecture.  Each tour may vary slightly\, depe
 nding on the tour guide.Know Before You GoAdmission and tours are free.Che
 ck in with Guest Services at least 5 minutes before the tour start time\, 
 to claim your reservation. At 1:25 p.m. any unclaimed spaces may be given 
 to guests who are waiting for a space.Read about where to find us\, where 
 to park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelines.To save time at the locker
 s\, avoid bringing backpacks or large bags.  When You ArriveCheck in with 
 Guest Services staff on the first floor by 1:25 p.m.Store any backpacks or
  large bags. Lockers and coatrack are available.Do not touch artwork. Be m
 indful to keep all body parts – and anything you're carrying – at leas
 t 18" (a half meter) away from artwork.Photography is welcome\, without fl
 ash or selfie stick.If you parked in the IMU parking lot\, Guest Services 
 can validate your parking voucher for a discount.    If this page says reg
 istration has closed\, this means the waitlist is full.  To request this t
 our at another time for a group of 6-24 people\, contact Laura at ematours
 @iu.edu (mailto:ematours@iu.edu).
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260805T202242Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2345843-public-tour-nature-inspired-
 art
