X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 261": "https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2364489-ai-literacy"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_261
SUMMARY:AI Literacy
DTSTART:20260908T140000Z
DTEND:20260908T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260729T131729Z
UID:20260908T140000Z-2364489@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260908T140000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1920,1920/31615_fall_into_research_livewhale_avatar.rev.1
 785270700.jpg
CATEGORIES:Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:This webinar breaks down what AI literacy actually means: the 
 ability to understand\, use\, monitor\, and critically reflect on AI appli
 cations with a goal towards understanding how these tools work\, where the
 y fall short\, and how to use them responsibly.We'll cover the basics of A
 I literacy\, how other literacy frameworks inform AI literacy\, and practi
 cal guidelines for responsible use\, including privacy\, bias\, IU specifi
 c policies\, and knowing whennotto use AI at all. Whether you're new to AI
  or already using it regularly\, you'll leave with a clearer framework for
  AI usage.__________  New to research\, new to managing your own data\, or
  interested in learning more about research data support at IU? Over the c
 ourse of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to walk yo
 u through the basics of researching with data at IU— from organizing and
  storing your data to meeting funder requirements and finding the right to
 ols.  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other ca
 mpus partners\, with sessions useful for researchers at any stage. Some se
 ssions may require advanced registration.  For any questions\, please cont
 act the IU Libraries Research Data Services team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:r
 esdata@iu.edu)) - and don't forget to check back regularly\, as new sessio
 ns are added!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901T212257Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2364489-ai-literacy
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="none">This webinar br
 eaks down what AI literacy actually means: the ability to understand\, use
 \, monitor\, and critically reflect on AI applications with a goal towards
  understanding how these tools work\, where they fall short\, and how to u
 se them responsibly.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;134233117&quot\;:
 false\,&quot\;134233118&quot\;:false\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&q
 uot\;335559738&quot\;:225\,&quot\;335559739&quot\;:225}"></span></p><p><sp
 an data-contrast="none">We'll cover the basics of AI literacy\, how other 
 literacy frameworks inform AI literacy\, and practical guidelines for resp
 onsible use\, including privacy\, bias\, IU specific policies\, and knowin
 g when</span><i><span data-contrast="none">not</span></i><span data-contra
 st="none">to use AI at all. Whether you're new to AI or already using it r
 egularly\, you'll leave with a clearer framework for AI usage.</span><span
  data-ccp-props="{&quot\;134233117&quot\;:false\,&quot\;134233118&quot\;:f
 alse\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559738&quot\;:0\,&quot\;
 335559739&quot\;:0}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="none">__________</
 span></p><p>  New to research\, new to managing your own data\, or interes
 ted in learning more about research data support at IU? Over the course of
  the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to walk you throug
 h the basics of researching with data at IU— from organizing and storing
  your data to meeting funder requirements and finding the right tools.</p>
 <p>  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other cam
 pus partners\, with sessions useful for researchers at any stage. Some ses
 sions may require advanced registration.</p><p>  For any questions\, pleas
 e contact the IU Libraries Research Data Services team (<a href="mailto:re
 sdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>) - and don't forget to check back regular
 ly\, as new sessions are added!</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  IU Libraries Research Data Services: <a hr
 ef="mailto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>&#160\;\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2364489
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1920\,1920/31615_fall_into_research_livewhal
 e_avatar.rev.1785270700.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-IS-ONLINE:1
X-LIVEWHALE-ONLINE-TYPE:Online only
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  <span class="TextRun SCXW232704674 BCX2" lang="
 EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="none"><span class="NormalTextRun SC
 XW232704674 BCX2">Artificial intelligence is now part of daily work\, and 
 even research. But using it well takes more than knowing how to type a pro
 mpt.</span></span>\n</p>
