BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 261": "https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2364492-teaching-data-with-icpsr-strategies-for-success-with"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_261
SUMMARY:Teaching Data with ICPSR: Strategies for Success with or without D
 ata
DTSTART:20260908T190000Z
DTEND:20260908T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260729T132043Z
UID:20260908T190000Z-2364492@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260908T190000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1920,1920/31615_fall_into_research_livewhale_avatar.rev.1
 785270700.jpg
CATEGORIES:Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:These thoughts go through everyone's heads when incorporating 
 something new into their teaching\, but exposing students to social scienc
 e data doesn't have to be onerous. This session will provide an overview o
 f the topics and types of data available from ICPSR (https://www.icpsr.umi
 ch.edu/sites/icpsr/home) and give you ideas for including data in class\, 
 sometimes without making students touch the data! ICPSR's search tools and
  the volume of data make it easy to match course concepts with real-world 
 examples. We'll also talk about what is and is not acceptable related to u
 sing ICPSR data in AI. And\, spoiler alert\, you don't have to be teaching
  research methods or statistics to include data!__________  New to researc
 h\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in learning more about r
 esearch data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, jo
 in us for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of researching 
 with data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to meeting funder
  requirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the I
 U Research Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions useful
  for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require advanced registra
 tion.  For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data S
 ervices team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don't forget t
 o check back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260811T235853Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2364492-teaching-data-with-icpsr
 -strategies-for-success-with
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="none">These thoughts 
 go through everyone's heads when incorporating something new into their te
 aching\, but exposing students to social science data doesn't have to be o
 nerous. This session will provide an overview of the topics and types of d
 ata available from <a href="https://www.icpsr.umich.edu/sites/icpsr/home">
 ICPSR</a> and give you ideas for including data in class\, sometimes witho
 ut making students touch the data! ICPSR's search tools and the volume of 
 data make it easy to match course concepts with real-world examples. We'll
  also talk about what is and is not acceptable related to using ICPSR data
  in AI. And\, spoiler alert\, you don't have to be teaching research metho
 ds or statistics to include data!</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;1342
 33117&quot\;:false\,&quot\;134233118&quot\;:false\,&quot\;335559738&quot\;
 :240\,&quot\;335559739&quot\;:0}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="none"
 >__________</span></p><p>  New to research\, new to managing your own data
 \, or interested in learning more about research data support at IU? Over 
 the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to wa
 lk you through the basics of researching with data at IU from organizing a
 nd storing your data to meeting funder requirements and finding the right 
 tools.</p><p>  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and
  other campus partners\, with sessions useful for researchers at any stage
 . Some sessions may require advanced registration.</p><p>  For any questio
 ns\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Services team (<a href=
 "mailto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>) - and don't forget to check ba
 ck regularly\, as new sessions are added!</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  IU Libraries Research Data Services: <a hr
 ef="mailto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>&#160\;\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2364492
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1920\,1920/31615_fall_into_research_livewhal
 e_avatar.rev.1785270700.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-IS-ONLINE:1
X-LIVEWHALE-ONLINE-TYPE:Online only
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  <span data-contrast="none">"I should use data i
 n my classes\, but…it's a lot of work\, I'm not an expert\, there's too 
 much else to talk about\, data are boring…"</span>\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TAGS:data|faculty|FallIntoResearch|graduate students|Research
