ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1920,1920/31615_fall_into_research_livewhale_avatar.rev.1
 785270700.jpg
CATEGORIES:Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:ICPSR (https://www.icpsr.umich.edu/sites/icpsr/home) is one of
  the largest archives for social and behavioral science data and\, with ov
 er 28\,000 studies\, there might just be something for you! This session w
 ill introduce you to the kinds of data in ICPSR's holdings\, provide searc
 h tips to help you find what you want\, and describe the standardized info
 rmation (metadata) you can use to evaluate whether the data will work for 
 your project. We'll talk about how to access both public use data\, availa
 ble with the push of a button or two\, and restricted data.__________  New
  to research\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in learning m
 ore about research data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 se
 mester\, join us for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of r
 esearching with data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to mee
 ting funder requirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Librar
 ies\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sess
 ions useful for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require advanc
 ed registration.  For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Rese
 arch Data Services team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don
 't forget to check back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260811T235818Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2364494-finding-and-evaluating-d
 ata-for-your-research
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="none"><a href="https:
 //www.icpsr.umich.edu/sites/icpsr/home">ICPSR</a> is one of the largest ar
 chives for social and behavioral science data and\, with over 28\,000 stud
 ies\, there might just be something for you! This session will introduce y
 ou to the kinds of data in ICPSR's holdings\, provide search tips to help 
 you find what you want\, and describe the standardized information (metada
 ta) you can use to evaluate whether the data will work for your project. W
 e'll talk about how to access both public use data\, available with the pu
 sh of a button or two\, and restricted data.</span><span data-ccp-props="{
 &quot\;134233117&quot\;:false\,&quot\;134233118&quot\;:false\,&quot\;33555
 9738&quot\;:240\,&quot\;335559739&quot\;:0}"></span></p><p><span data-cont
 rast="none">__________</span></p><p>  New to research\, new to managing yo
 ur own data\, or interested in learning more about research data support a
 t IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars des
 igned to walk you through the basics of researching with data at IU— fro
 m organizing and storing your data to meeting funder requirements and find
 ing the right tools.</p><p>  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data
  Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions useful for researcher
 s at any stage. Some sessions may require advanced registration.</p><p>  F
 or any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Services 
 team (<a href="mailto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>) - and don't forg
 et to check back regularly\, as new sessions are added!</p>
