 </td></tr><tr><td colspan="2"><p style="text-align: center\;">          &#
 160\;        </p><p style="text-align: center\;"><strong><em>By Their Own 
 Hands: The Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame!</em></strong></p><p>          Fo
 unded in 1974 by the Culture and Ethnic Affairs Guild of the Oakland Museu
 m of California\, the Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame began as a film lectur
 e series and awards ceremony celebrating achievements of Black film indust
 ry figures. When that organization closed\, they donated their materials t
 o IU. In collaboration with the IU Black Film Center and Archive\, this ex
 hibit features objects from that collection\, including founding documents
 \, costumes\, and handprints of inductees to the Hall of Fame.        </p>
 <p style="text-align: center\;"><strong>Dates: September 2025 - December 2
 026</strong></p><p>          &#160\;        </p><picture class="lw_image l
 w_image28163  lw_align_center"><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://e
 vents.iu.edu/live/image/gid/479/width/250/height/125/28163_27301_3_handpri
 nts.rev.1758043255.webp 1x" data-origin="responsive"/><source type="image/
 png" srcset="https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/479/width/250/height/125
 /28163_27301_3_handprints.rev.1758043255.png 1x" data-origin="responsive"/
 ><img alt="" width="250" height="125" data-alt="" data-decoration="true" s
 rc="https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/479/width/250/height/125/28163_27
 301_3_handprints.rev.1758043255.png" title="27301 3 handprints.rev.1754064
 868" data-max-w="250" data-max-h="125" loading="lazy" data-optimized="true
 "/></picture></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 99.9123%\;" colspan="2"><p st
 yle="text-align: center\;">          &#160\;        </p><p style="text-ali
 gn: center\;"><strong><em>Capturing the Campus: T.C. Steele\, Indiana Univ
 ersity's First Artist in Residence</em></strong></p><p><em>Capturing the C
 ampus</em> pays tribute to renowned Hoosier artist T.C. Steele. The exhibi
 t honors the century that has passed since his death by showcasing paintin
 gs form the artist's residency at IU and other relevant works. The exhibit
  will bring together Steele's landscapes from the IU Public Art and Cultur
 al Heritage Collection and the Indiana State Museum and Historic Sites' co
 llection\, allowing the holdings of these two collections to be viewed in 
 one space.        </p><p style="text-align: center\;"><strong>Dates: April
  17\, 2026 - April 2026</strong></p><p><picture class="lw_image lw_image30
 589  lw_align_left"><source media="(max-width: 500px)" type="image/webp" s
 rcset="https://events.iu.edu/live/image/scale/2x/gid/479/width/500/height/
 350/30589_CC279_public_access.rev.1774288720.webp 2x" data-origin="respons
 ive"/><source media="(max-width: 500px)" type="image/jpeg" srcset="https:/
 /events.iu.edu/live/image/scale/2x/gid/479/width/500/height/350/30589_CC27
