CATEGORIES:Fundraiser/Philanthropy
CATEGORIES:Other
CATEGORIES:Campus-Wide Event
DESCRIPTION:ACC is co-sponsoring this event with Nepali Student Associatio
 n\, Union Board and APA Staff & Faculty Council.\n \nJoin us for a specia
 l benefit gathering to support long-term relief and rebuilding efforts in
  Nepal. The event will take place on Wednesday\, September 9\, 2026\, fro
 m 4:30 PM to 5:30 PM at the Maxwell Hall Cook Center. This gathering is c
 o-sponsored by the Asian Culture Center\, the Asian Pacific American Facu
 lty and Staff Council\, and the Nepali Student Association. (Online link 
 will be posted soon!)\n\n\n \nOn August 26\, 2026\, a massive glacier col
 lapse near the China–Nepal border triggered catastrophic flash floods and
  debris flows along the Trishuli River basin. The surge swept away entire
  towns\, critical bridges\, and essential border infrastructure\, claimin
 g over 1\,200 lives and leaving thousands missing. Nearly 25 miles of roa
 d and 32 bridges were destroyed across steep\, remote districts\, making 
 physical reconstruction a long and hazardous effort. The threat of repeat
  glacial- and landslide-triggered floods is high.\n \nThe September 9 gat
 hering will feature personal perspectives from members of the IU Blooming
 ton Nepali community alongside expert insights from Dr. Brian Yanites\, a
 n IU geologist specializing in landslides who has been closely monitoring
  the disaster. Volunteers will be available throughout the event to guide
  attendees on how to make direct monetary donations to relief efforts.\n 
 \nIU Bloomington shares a deep and lasting connection with Nepal. Nobel l
 aureate Elinor Ostrom brought global attention to the Himalayan nation th
 rough her seminal research on its community-managed resources\, and IU st
 udents continue to visit Nepal through annual literary and cultural excha
 nges.\n \nWe hope you can join us in demonstrating our campus community's
  care and commitment to Nepal during this critical time.\n \n\n\nAll Indi
 ana University events\, groups\, activities\, and educational\, cultural\
 , and historical observances welcome all IU students and other members of
  the Indiana University community.\n\nHosted by: Asian Culture Center\, I
 ndiana Memorial Union Board\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: ht
 tps://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12703944
DTEND:20260909T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041536Z
DTSTART:20260909T203000Z
GEO:39.166900;-86.524760
LOCATION:The Cook Center in Maxwell Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Help Nepal: A Community Forum and Fundraiser for Nepali Flood Vict
 ims
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12703944
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12703944
X-HOSTS:Indiana Memorial Union Board
END:VEVENT
