 1/src_region/0,0,1081,1081/31448_HSD-FullColor.rev.1783430812.png
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by artworks in the galleries\, students will explore 
 how meaning can be built through design and structure. Join us to create y
 our own mini slot sculpture pillar that celebrates the people\, traditions
 \, and values that make up who you are!  Program designed by our licensed 
 art educator for students in grades K-12.Know Before You Go:  Meet us in t
 he Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the museum at 1 pm. To
 gether\, we'll drop off personal items before exploring the galleries.&#16
 0\; After seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll head back 
 to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own masterpieces! Don'
 t forget to dress for a mess!  Strollers are welcome. Chaperone required. 
 We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult for every 6 childre
 n.
