 aditions
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Inspired by artworks in the galleries\, 
 students will explore how meaning can be built through design and structur
 e. Join us to create your own mini slot sculpture pillar that celebrates t
 he people\, traditions\, and values that make up who you are!</p><p>  Prog
 ram designed by our licensed art educator for students in grades K-12.</p>
 <p><strong>Know Before You Go:</strong></p><p>  Meet us in the Simpson Cen
 ter for Education on the 2nd floor of the museum at 1 pm. Together\, we'll
  drop off personal items before exploring the galleries.&#160\; After seei
 ng artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll head back to the Roehm F
 amily Art-Making Studio to create our own masterpieces! Don't forget to dr
 ess for a mess!</p><p>  Strollers are welcome. <strong>Chaperone required.
 </strong> We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult for every
  6 children.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  <strong>Madelyn Cage</strong><br />\n  You
 th and Family Art Education Manager<br />\n  Sidney and Lois Eskenazi Muse
 um of Art<br />\n  <a href="mailto:cagem@iu.edu">cagem@iu.edu<br />\n  812
 -855-0607</a>\n</p>
