 mysterious potion bottles\, take a stab at felting a miniature art piece\
 , design your own folk creature mask\, and more!    </p><p>      This pro
 gram is free and open to all\, with Museum galleries remaining open for t
 he entirety of the event to give a special\, after-hours view of the exhi
 bitions.    </p></div>&#160\;</div><p><strong>Parking Information:</stron
 g></p><p><span data-contrast="auto">Limited</span><span data-contrast="au
 to">complimentary parking</span><span data-contrast="auto">is available i
 n front of the</span><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/k4Txsojst2gSW5fUA">
 <span data-contrast="none">Museum entrance</span></a><span data-contrast=
 "auto">off Indiana Avenue. Street parking is free on weekdays after 5:00 
 PM in the neighborhoods surrounding the Museum. Paid parking options incl
 ude the</span><span data-contrast="none"></span><a href="https://maps.app
 .goo.gl/3i62KNcjDeCACruHA"><span data-contrast="none">University Collecti
 ons at McCalla</span></a><span data-contrast="auto">parking lot off India
 na Avenue\, the</span><span data-contrast="none"></span><a href="https://
