BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Browncounty": "https://browncountyartguild.org/art-colony-weekend/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:browncounty
SUMMARY:Brown County Art Colony Weekend 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260911T040000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260914T040000
DTSTAMP:20260902T152020Z
UID:MEC-cd87e2bc6b55c371e7cd41fc79550531@browncounty.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260911T040000
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 09/acw26_web_event-1024x576-1.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art Events &amp\; Exhibits,Special Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260902
DESCRIPTION:Immerse yourself in Brown County’s creative spirit during Ar
 t Colony Weekend\, September 11–13\, 2026. This three-day celebration in
 vites art enthusiasts of all ages to explore the history\, artists and nat
 ural beauty that helped establish Brown County as one of America’s most 
 celebrated art colonies.\nTour Nashville’s galleries\, admire historic a
 nd contemporary works\, watch artists paint outdoors\, contribute to a com
 munity masterpiece and discover a special piece to take home during the Br
 own County Art Colony Auction.\nFriday\, September 11\nFounders Exhibition
 : Frederick W. Rigley\n11 a.m.–7 p.m. | Brown County Art Guild\nView a r
 are collection honoring founding artist Frederick W. Rigley and his apprec
 iation for the landscapes\, light and character of southern Indiana.\nGall
 ery Hop\n5–7 p.m. | Downtown Nashville\nTour participating galleries thr
 oughout the village while enjoying live painting\, music\, refreshments an
 d artwork available for purchase.\nSaturday\, September 12\nGreat Outdoor 
 Art Contest\n7 a.m.–4 p.m. | T.C. Steele State Historic Site\nIndiana’
 s oldest plein-air painting competition celebrates its 38th year. Watch ar
 tists work throughout the day\, followed by judging at 2 p.m. and award an
 nouncements beginning at 3:30 p.m. A separate site admission fee applies.\
 nCommunity Paint Together\nNoon–4 p.m. | Village Green at Main and Jeffe
 rson Streets\nArtists of every age and experience level are invited to hel
 p create a collaborative community masterpiece. Families are welcome.\nBro
 wn County Art Gallery\n10 a.m.–5 p.m. | One Artist Drive\nExplore “The
 odore Clement Steele: Indiana’s Master Impressionist from Munich to Brow
 n County.” At 2 p.m.\, enjoy a live performance of “Selma and the Pain
 ter\,” featuring Broadway actress Jill Tasker as Selma Steele. Seating i
 s limited.\nArt Colony Auction Preview\n10 a.m.–1 p.m. | Brown County In
 n\nPreview the artwork that will be featured in Sunday’s Brown County Ar
 t Colony Auction.\nGuild Speaker Series: Rick Kelley\n1–2:30 p.m. | Brow
 n County Inn\nBrown County historian Rick Kelley shares stories and insigh
 ts about the artists\, places and events that shaped the Brown County Art 
 Colony. A question-and-answer session will follow.\nSunday\, September 13\
 nBrown County Art Colony Auction\nPreview: 11 a.m.–1 p.m.\nAuction: 1–
 4:30 p.m.\nBrown County Inn\nExperience a lively afternoon of bidding feat
 uring historic works by Midwest Art Colony artists alongside pieces from a
 ward-winning contemporary artists.\nEvents are free and open to the public
  unless otherwise noted. For additional information\, visit browncountyart
 guild.org or call 812-988-6185.\n \n \n \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260902
ORGANIZER;CN="Brown County Art Guild":MAILTO:admin@bcartguild.org
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://browncountyartguild.org/art-colony-weekend/
X-SOURCE:Brown County Events
END:VEVENT
