CATEGORIES:Career development,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,S
 tudent-run,Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:The Diplomacy Lab is a practitioner-led partnership that allow
 s the Hamilton Lugar School to provide direct analysis for the U.S. Depart
 ment of State. This isn't just a research project—it's a chance to consu
 lt on urgent global challenges\, from climate security to digital freedom\
 , directly from Bloomington.  Join us on September 11 for a strategic brie
 fing on the Spring 2027 cycle. We will move beyond the syllabus to show yo
 u how to form a team\, align with faculty expertise\, and submit a winning
  bid.What we will cover:The Matchmaking Strategy: Using our internal inter
 est lists to pair student technical skills with faculty subject-matter exp
 ertise.    The Bidding Mechanics: A step-by-step guide to the project menu
  and the requirements for faculty-led submissions.    The 3-Credit Standar
 d: Why we are standardizing the Lab experience to ensure professional pari
 ty and academic rigor.    Lessons Learned: A panel of HLS faculty and stud
 ents will discuss their experiences managing previous teams and project ID
 s.    Who should attend?Faculty looking to integrate practitioner-led trad
 ecraft into their research.    Students eager to build a professional port
 folio of "Day 1" assets.
