X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 130": "https://events.iu.edu/cahi/event/2394812-cahi-humanities-hangout-with-dr-richard-gunderman"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_130
SUMMARY:CAHI Humanities Hangout with Dr. Richard Gunderman
DTSTART:20260911T200000Z
DTEND:20260911T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260825T143139Z
UID:20260911T200000Z-2394812@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260911T200000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/130/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,400,500/32196_trustee-richard-gunderman.rev.1787682300.jp
 g
CATEGORIES:Career development,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Are you pre-med\, or interested in going into a medical field 
 and also interested in doing a major or minor in the humanities?  If so\, 
 please join us for a Humanities Hangout on Friday\, September 11\, at 4 pm
  in GISB 1118\, with Dr. Richard B. Gunderman\, MD\, PhD.  Dr. Gunderman i
 s a distinguished professor of Radiology\, Pediatrics\, Philanthropy\, Phi
 losophy\, and Medical Humanities at the Indiana University School of Medic
 ine.  He will answer questions about how his training in the humanities is
  an important part of his career now as a physician\, professor\, and auth
 or of numerous books.  Dr. Gunderman is a dynamic speaker and acclaimed te
 acher—so much so that he received the Indiana University School of Medic
 ine's inaugural Inspirational Educator Award in 2015.  Come see how explor
 ing your interests in the humanities can help make you a better doctor and
  medical professional!  Pizza will be served.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260825T183139Z
LOCATION:GISB
URL:https://events.iu.edu/cahi/event/2394812-cahi-humanities-hangout-with-
 dr-richard-gunderman
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Are you pre-m
 ed\, or interested in going into a medical field and also interested in do
 ing a major or minor in the humanities?</p><p style="font-weight: 400\;"> 
  If so\, please join us for a Humanities Hangout on Friday\, September 11\
 , at 4 pm in GISB 1118\, with Dr. Richard B. Gunderman\, MD\, PhD.</p><p s
 tyle="font-weight: 400\;">  Dr. Gunderman is a distinguished professor of 
 Radiology\, Pediatrics\, Philanthropy\, Philosophy\, and Medical Humanitie
 s at the Indiana University School of Medicine.</p><p style="font-weight: 
 400\;">  He will answer questions about how his training in the humanities
  is an important part of his career now as a physician\, professor\, and a
 uthor of numerous books.</p><p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Dr. Gunderman 
 is a dynamic speaker and acclaimed teacher—so much so that he received t
 he Indiana University School of Medicine's inaugural Inspirational Educato
 r Award in 2015.</p><p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Come see how exploring
  your interests in the humanities can help make you a better doctor and me
 dical professional!</p><p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Pizza will be serve
 d.</p>
