CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Since 2016\, Gunn has been Education Director at the Tamarind 
 Institute\, a globally recognized center for fine art lithography in Albuq
 uerque\, New Mexico. He is also the owner of arcEditions\, a premier U.S. 
 maker of leather rollers.Gunn has taught printmaking at IU Bloomington\, C
 oncordia University (Montreal)\, and Brigham Young University (BYU)-Idaho 
 and has consulted with institutions including the Roswell Artist-in-Reside
 nce Program (N.M.)\, Santa Reparata (Florence\, Italy)\, and BYU to design
  studios\, streamline workflows\, and integrate lithography into their pro
 grams. He has also collaborated with manufacturers such as Takach Press (A
 lbuquerque) and Cranfield Colours (Wales\, UK) to develop and ensure relia
 ble\, high-quality materials for the field.  &#160\;The McKinney Visiting 
 Artist Series brings prominent working artists from a range of studio prac
 tices and fields to the Eskenazi School of Art\, Architecture + Design. Ar
 tists lead workshops and critiques for students within the department\, as
  well as lectures and gallery talks open to the campus community.The Colle
 ge of Arts and Sciences and the Eskenazi School of Art\, Architecture + De
 sign gratefully acknowledge Dr. Meredith McKinney (B.A. '65) and Elsa Luis
 e Barthel McKinney (B.A. '65) for their love of the arts and their generou
 s support in endowing the McKinney Visiting Artist Series at Indiana Unive
 rsity Bloomington.
GEO:39.169084;-86.518997
LAST-MODIFIED:20260818T200027Z
LOCATION:Fine Arts Building\, 1201 East 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 4740
 5
URL:https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2385173-brandon-gunn-mckinney-vis
 iting-artist-series-lecture
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="none">Since 2016\, Gu
 nn has been Education Director at the Tamarind Institute\, a globally reco
 gnized center for fine art lithography in Albuquerque\, New Mexico. He is 
 also the owner of arcEditions\, a premier U.S. maker of leather rollers.</
 span><span data-ccp-props="{}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="none">Gu
 nn has taught printmaking at IU Bloomington\, Concordia University (Montre
 al)\, and Brigham Young University (BYU)-Idaho and has consulted with inst
 itutions including the Roswell Artist-in-Residence Program (N.M.)\, Santa 
 Reparata (Florence\, Italy)\, and BYU to design studios\, streamline workf
 lows\, and integrate lithography into their programs. He has also collabor
 ated with manufacturers such as Takach Press (Albuquerque) and Cranfield C
 olours (Wales\, UK) to develop and ensure reliable\, high-quality material
 s for the field.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;134233117&quot\;:fals
 e\,&quot\;134233118&quot\;:false\,&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335551
