BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Brown County State Park": "https://on.in.gov/browncountysp"}
X-SOURCE-ID:localist_brown_county_sp
SUMMARY:Timber! Understanding the Timber Rattlesnake\, Brown County State 
 Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260912T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260912T133000
UID:8145f5e36d725d7b8b7a97940c753a4d@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Come to the Nature Center for an up close and personal look In
 diana&#39\;s most venomous and most misunderstood snake! Learn about the h
 istory of timber rattlesnakes\, including how this animal became an Americ
 an symbol in the late 1700s. Learn how over a million visitors a year safe
 ly share the state park with these animals. We&#39\;ll also discuss venom\
 , how it works and is delievered\, and how Indiana&#39\;s venomous snakes 
 compare to the rest of the world! At the end\, we will feed the timber rat
 tlesnake a live mouse. Please be aware this program involves live animals.
  A live snake feeding may not be suitable for all guests\, particuarly chi
 ldren. Guests will have an opportunity to leave the program before the fee
 ding\, if they choose to do so. The program room has seating for about 45 
 people maximum. On busy days\, it is wise to arrive early!
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Bloomspinweave": "https://bloomspinweave.org/event/beginning-sock-knitting-with-yvonne-jones-week-4"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bloomspinweave
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Spinners & Weavers Guild
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260912T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260912T160000
DTSTAMP:20260819T131718Z
CREATED:20260429T185343Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260819T131718Z
UID:6536-1789218000-1789228800@bloomspinweave.org
SUMMARY:Beginning Sock Knitting with Yvonne Jones\, Week 4
DESCRIPTION:You’ve learned to knit so now what?  Well\, let’s knit some socks!  This workshop will be for the very beginner sock knitter\, but suitable if you are a cuff-down sock knitter and would like to try toe-up.  We will talk about different types of sock\, heel\, and toe construction\, then we will CAST-ON for a Beginner TOE-UP MAGIC LOOP Sock! \nThe workshop will take place over 4 weeks; Saturdays\, August 22\, August 29\, September 5\, & September 12\, 2026. 1:00- 4:00 PM each day. \nWeek 4: We will talk about different types of bind offs and choose one that has enough stretch to get your sock onto your foot\, then knit the cuff and finish your sock. \nREGISTRATION CLOSED \n\n           Download QR
URL:https://bloomspinweave.org/event/beginning-sock-knitting-with-yvonne-jones-week-4
CATEGORIES:Bloomington Spinners and Weavers Fiber Arts Guild Calendar
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bloomspinweave.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/0822-0905-Sock-Workshop-Yvonne-Jones-CROPPED.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Brown County Art Guild": "https://browncountyartguild.org/event/guild-speaker-series/", "Limestone Post": "https://browncountyartguild.org/event/guild-speaker-series/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Browncountyartguild": "https://browncountyartguild.org/event/guild-speaker-series/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:browncountyartguild
X-SOURCE:Brown County Art Guild, Limestone Post
DTSTART;TZID=UTC:20260912T130000
DTEND;TZID=UTC:20260912T143000
DTSTAMP:20260819T182110Z
CREATED:20260818T134931Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260819T182110Z
UID:33589-1789218000-1789223400@browncountyartguild.org
SUMMARY:Guild Speaker Series
DESCRIPTION:Rick Kelley \nBrown County Art History/Q&A\nSaturday\, September 12\n1pm – 2:30pm \nBrown County Inn  \nAs part of the 2026 Art Colony Weekend and in conjunction with the Art Colony Auction Preview\, join us for a fascinating journey into the history of one of America’s most celebrated art colonies. \nBrown County historian and resident Rick Kelley will share his deep knowledge of the Brown County Art Colony and the remarkable artists who came to these hills seeking inspiration\, community\, and a place to call home. Through engaging stories\, personal insights\, and historical anecdotes\, Rick brings the past to life\, revealing the people\, places\, and events that shaped Brown County’s rich artistic legacy. Rick will invite audience members to ask questions and share in the conversation. \nThis event is free and open to the public.
URL:https://browncountyartguild.org/event/guild-speaker-series/
CATEGORIES:Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncountyartguild.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/speakers_series_web_event.jpg
END:VEVENT
