X-SOURCE-ID:browncounty
SUMMARY:T.C. Steele Centennial Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260913T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260913T210000
DTSTAMP:20260626T114759Z
UID:MEC-ddec43d1aaf5430b765eb939ca392bba@browncounty.com__20260913
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/
 09/Art-Gallery-Exterior-Listing.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art Events &amp\; Exhibits,Happening
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260626
DESCRIPTION:On July 18th\, be the first to see this once in a lifetime exh
 ibition of Indiana’s premier Hoosier Master\, Theodore Clement Steele.\n
 Seventy paintings that span his revered career will fill the walls of the 
 historic Brown County Art in memoriam of Steele’s passing in 1926 and th
 e founding of the Gallery by the artists who followed him to Brown County.
 \nPaintings come from private and public collections and have rarely been 
 seen by the public. A full color catalogue features each painting and Stee
 le’s extensive exhibition history. It’s a must have for both the patro
 n and the educator. Copies are $25 but one will be included with each open
 ing night reservation.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260626
LOCATION:One Artist Drive. Nashville\, Indiana
ORGANIZER;CN="Historic Brown County Art Gallery":MAILTO:
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/t-c-steele-centennial-exhibit/
X-SOURCE:Brown County Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Butlerwinery": "https://butlerwinery.com/event/sunday-live-music-sotto-voce-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:butlerwinery
X-SOURCE:Butler Winery
DTSTART;TZID=UTC:20260913T140000
DTEND;TZID=UTC:20260913T170000
DTSTAMP:20260513T205521Z
CREATED:20260513T205521Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260513T205521Z
UID:12840-1789308000-1789318800@butlerwinery.com
SUMMARY:Sunday Live Music: SOTTO VOCE
DESCRIPTION:The Sotto Voce Jazz Quintet focuses on the music of the Great American Songbook\, with the music of Cole Porter\, Hoagy Carmichael\, George Gershwin\, Duke Ellington\, and other familiar 20th Century composers. “Sotto Voce” in Italian means “Subdued Voice”\, and the quintet aims to provide familiar tunes in a comfortable aural setting. The quintet is comprised of experienced local players: Angie Aumage on vocals and guitar\, Rich Pierce on guitar\, Paulo Dias on piano\, Randy Gratz on bass\, and Dave Shank on drums.
URL:https://butlerwinery.com/event/sunday-live-music-sotto-voce-2/
END:VEVENT
