DESCRIPTION:Join the American Constitution Society\, the Federalist Societ
 y\, and the Maurer School of Law for a conversation on the scope of presid
 ential authority over war powers\, featuring guest speakers Robert F. Turn
 er and Scott R. Anderson.  RSVP below by 4 pm on Friday\, September 11 to 
 attend.  Food will be provided to those who RSVP.&#160\;__________________
 ____________________________________________Robert F. Turner was a co-foun
 der\, Distinguished Fellow\, and Professor at the University of Virginia's
  Center for National Security Law. He was also the Charles H. Stockton Cha
 ir of International Law at the U.S. Naval War College. Professor Turner cu
 rrently serves as a nonresident senior fellow at George Mason University's
  National Security Institute.Scott R. Anderson is a Senior Fellow in Gover
 nance Studies at the Brookings Institution and General Counsel and Senior 
 Editor at Lawfare. He is also a nonresident Senior Fellow with the Nationa
 l Security Program at Columbia Law School. Previously\, Anderson served as
  an attorney-adviser for the U.S. Department of State and as the legal adv
 iser for the U.S. Embassy in Baghdad\, Iraq.&#160\;
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T190957Z
LOCATION:Lowell E. Baier Hall - DeLaney Moot Court Room - 123
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2401706-hold-constitution-day-progr
 am
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join the American Constitution Society\,
  the Federalist Society\, and the Maurer School of Law for a conversation 
 on the scope of presidential authority over war powers\, featuring guest s
 peakers Robert F. Turner and Scott R. Anderson.</p><p>  RSVP below by 4 pm
  on Friday\, September 11 to attend.</p><p>  Food will be provided to thos
 e who RSVP.&#160\;</p><p><strong>_________________________________________
 _____________________</strong></p><p><strong>Robert F. Turner</strong> was
  a co-founder\, Distinguished Fellow\, and Professor at the University of 
 Virginia's Center for National Security Law. He was also the Charles H. St
 ockton Chair of International Law at the U.S. Naval War College. Professor
  Turner currently serves as a nonresident senior fellow at George Mason Un
 iversity's National Security Institute.</p><p><strong>Scott R. Anderson</s
 trong> is a Senior Fellow in Governance Studies at the Brookings Instituti
 on and General Counsel and Senior Editor at Lawfare. He is also a nonresid
 ent Senior Fellow with the National Security Program at Columbia Law Schoo
 l. Previously\, Anderson served as an attorney-adviser for the U.S. Depart
 ment of State and as the legal adviser for the U.S. Embassy in Baghdad\, I
 raq.&#160\;</p>
