SUMMARY:Protecting Human Participants and the IRB Process
DTSTART:20260916T180000Z
DTEND:20260916T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260729T133225Z
UID:20260916T180000Z-2364498@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260916T180000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1920,1920/31615_fall_into_research_livewhale_avatar.rev.1
 785270700.jpg
CATEGORIES:Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Learn more about the review process at IU — including requir
 ed trainings\, typical timelines\, required documentation\, and what const
 itutes 'human participant research' — to understand how IRB review prote
 cts participants while supporting meaningful research.__________  New to r
 esearch\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in learning more a
 bout research data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semeste
 r\, join us for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of resear
 ching with data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to meeting 
 funder requirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries\,
  the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions 
 useful for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require advanced re
 gistration.  For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research 
 Data Services team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don't fo
 rget to check back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260811T235548Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2364498-protecting-human-partici
 pants-and-the-irb-process
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="none">Learn more abou
 t the review process at IU — including required trainings\, typical time
 lines\, required documentation\, and what constitutes 'human participant r
 esearch' — to understand how IRB review protects participants while supp
 orting meaningful research.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;134233117&
 quot\;:false\,&quot\;134233118&quot\;:false\,&quot\;335559738&quot\;:240\,
 &quot\;335559739&quot\;:0}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="none">_____
 _____</span></p><p>  New to research\, new to managing your own data\, or 
 interested in learning more about research data support at IU? Over the co
 urse of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to walk you
  through the basics of researching with data at IU— from organizing and 
 storing your data to meeting funder requirements and finding the right too
 ls.</p><p>  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and ot
 her campus partners\, with sessions useful for researchers at any stage. S
 ome sessions may require advanced registration.</p><p>  For any questions\
 , please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Services team (<a href="ma
 ilto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>) - and don't forget to check back 
 regularly\, as new sessions are added!</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  IU Libraries Research Data Services: <a hr
 ef="mailto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>&#160\;\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
