SUMMARY:Aim for Advocacy: A Happy Hour with Monroe County CASA
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T190000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041504Z
UID:nr1ogkqj0nimhi33f3mo46s0q8@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T170000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260806T130737Z
DESCRIPTION:Strike up some fun and aim for change. Join us for a fun-fille
 d happy hour at Hoosier Alley\, supporting Monroe County CASA. Whether you
  know about CASA or are new to the work they do\, you can have some fun wh
 ile showing up for abused and neglected kids in our community.\n\n$25 incl
 udes VIP bowling\, ax throwing\, and a pizza buffet. Cash bar available.\n
 \n$25 per person | 18+ | Tickets close September 15\nTickets: https://bit.
 ly/aimforadvocacy\n\nSponsored by IU Credit Union and Hoosier Alley.\n\nAb
 out Monroe County CASA: Monroe County CASA\, Inc. is a nonprofit organizat
 ion that recruits\, trains\, and supervises court-appointed volunteers who
  advocate for children involved in the legal system due to abuse or neglec
 t.\n\nContact: Amber Shride\, 812-333-2272\, amber.shride@monroecountycasa
 .org
LAST-MODIFIED:20260806T130854Z
LOCATION:Hoosier Alley Entertainment\, 2424 S Walnut St\, Bloomington\, IN
  47401\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:BloomingtonOnline Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Libcal Iub 1228": "https://iub.libcal.com/event/17492318"}
X-SOURCE-ID:libcal_iub_1228
X-SOURCE:Libcal Iub 1228
DTSTART:20260917T170000Z
DTEND:20260917T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260917T000000Z
SUMMARY:Scholarly Write-In
DESCRIPTION:Write and work in solidarity with other IU scholars. We offer a 
 silent work environment with coffee and natural light. The write-in is open 
 to all graduate students (at any stage of their degree program).\n\n \n\nWe 
 will check in at the beginning of our meeting\, set some goals together\, 
 then work independently for a few hours. Fifteen minutes prior to the close 
 of the meeting\, we will reconvene to update each other on our progress and 
 set broad goals for the coming week.\n\nThis is a casual meeting – feel 
 free to come for as much or as little time as you like\, and only during 
 the weeks that work for you. You are welcome and encouraged to work on 
 anything that you need time and space for: participants regularly work on 
 dissertations\, course papers\, syllabi and lesson plans\, articles and 
 pieces for publication\, and grading. Our goal is to create a space where 
 we can work together in solidarity on whatever projects we need to each 
 week.\n\nMeets weekly throughout the semester\, Thursday from 1-3pm. No 
 meeting during Thanksgiving break.\n\nCo-sponsored by Writing Tutorial 
 Services and the IU Libraries.\n
LOCATION:IQ Wall- E157H
ORGANIZER;CN="Alyssa Denneler":MAILTO:alydenn@iu.edu
CATEGORIES:Citing, Writing & Research Tools
UID:LibCal-1228-17492318
URL:https://iub.libcal.com/event/17492318
END:VEVENT
