DESCRIPTION:5:00–7:00 p.m. | Opening reception\,hors d'oeuvres and cash 
 bar\, 2nd floor atriumAbout the Artist:  Known for his large-scale abstrac
 t assemblages made from deconstructed encyclopedias\, law books\, medical 
 texts\, and other printed materials\, Jones transforms sources of institut
 ional knowledge into richly textured works that question how information\,
 history\,andauthorityareconstructed.Bydismantlingandreconstructingthesemat
 erials\,hisworkexaminessystemsthatshapeculturalnarratives\,power\,andprivi
 legeintheUnitedStates.DrawinginspirationfromtheideasofFrenchphilosopherMic
 helFoucault\,SamuelLeviJones:AnArchaeologyofKnowledge brings together work
 s spanning ten years of Jones's practice. For this presentation\, Jones al
 so engaged with the Eskenazi Museum of Art's collection\,identifyingworkst
 hatresonatewiththemescentraltohisresearch\,includingnationalismandpatrioti
 sm\,censorship\,andtherepresentationofmarginalizedidentitiesinhistoricalna
 rratives.  For more information including museum location\, where to park\
 , accessibility\, and museum guidelines.
