SUMMARY:Your DC Moment | Dinner with Ambassador and Professor Lee Feinstei
 n
DTSTART:20260917T213000Z
DTEND:20260917T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260707T094219Z
UID:20260917T213000Z-2344613@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260917T213000Z
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,Student-run,Training
 , non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Attend an exclusive working dinner and strategy session for th
 e Spring 2027 D.C. Global Policy Program. Don't just study global leadersh
 ip. Put it into practice.  This intimate event is for students interested 
 in the Hamilton Lugar Spring 2027 residency. It's a working dinner and a p
 eek at what a global career actually feels like before you step into it.Wh
 y you should attend:Sit at the Table: Engage with a leader who has shaped 
 global policy and his international career.  Alumni Insights: Hear from a 
 panel of D.C. Program alumni regarding their on-the-ground experiences.  T
 he Professional Roadmap: Get a technical walkthrough of the Spring 2027 cy
 cle\, including the January 11 – May 7 residency dates.  Logistics Bridg
 e: Understand how the IU Capital Campus housing works and how the classes 
 work for undergrads\, grad\, and PhD students.  The AgendaI. The Practitio
 ner Perspective: A briefing from Ambassador Lee Feinstein on D.C. professi
 onal realities and "tradecraft" skills.II. The Roadmap: A deep dive into t
 he October 15 deadline\, interview sprints (Oct 26–28)\, and the mandato
 ry December 12 orientation.III. Housing &amp\; Classes: Guidance on the Ca
 pital Campus residency and the academic courses offered in D.C.IV. Ground 
 Game: Peer-to-peer breakouts and alumni panel discussion on commuting\, an
 d professional life in DC.Can't make the full hour? No problem. This is a 
 come-and-go strategy session designed to fit your Thursday schedule.Link t
 o Application: https://iu.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_bxucZoEtLdi24a (ht
 tps://iu.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_bxucZoEtLdi24aW)___________________
 _____________________________________Biography: Ambassador &amp\; Professo
 r Lee Feinstein  Ambassador Lee Feinstein is a Senior Managing Director an
 d the President of McLarty Associates. He previously served as the U.S. Am
 bassador to the Republic of Poland and held senior positions at the Depart
 ment of State\, including Principal Deputy Director and a Member of the Po
 licy Planning Staff. He was the Founding Dean of the Hamilton Lugar School
  of Global and International Studies at Indiana University from 2014 to 20
 22. Ambassador Feinstein is a member of the Council on Foreign Relations a
 nd the American Academy of Diplomacy\, and holds a JD from Georgetown Univ
 ersity Law Center.
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20260819T163501Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2296369-your-dc-moment-dinner-with-a
 mbassador-and
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p class="intro" data-path-to-node="5"><img s
 rc="https://internationalstudies.indiana.edu/images/people/profiles/feinst
 ein-lee.jpg" alt="Lee Feinstein: Faculty: People: International Studies: I
 ndiana University Bloomington" loading="lazy"/></p><p class="intro" data-p
 ath-to-node="5">  Attend an exclusive working dinner and strategy session 
 for the Spring 2027 D.C. Global Policy Program. <span style="text-decorati
 on: underline\;"><em>Don't just study global leadership. Put it into pract
 ice.</em></span></p><p class="intro" data-path-to-node="5">  This intimate
  event is for students interested in the Hamilton Lugar Spring 2027 reside
 ncy. It's a working dinner and a peek at what a global career actually fee
 ls like before you step into it.</p><p class="intro" data-path-to-node="7"
 ><strong data-path-to-node="7" data-index-in-node="0">Why you should atten
 d:</strong></p><ul><li data-path-to-node="8\,0\,0"><strong data-path-to-no
 de="8\,0\,0" data-index-in-node="0">Sit at the Table:</strong> Engage with
  a leader who has shaped global policy and his international career.  </li
 ><li data-path-to-node="8\,0\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="8\,1\,0" data-
 index-in-node="0">Alumni Insights:</strong> Hear from a panel of D.C. Prog
 ram alumni regarding their on-the-ground experiences.  </li><li data-path-
 to-node="8\,0\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="8\,2\,0" data-index-in-node="
 0">The Professional Roadmap:</strong> Get a technical walkthrough of the S
 pring 2027 cycle\, including the <strong data-path-to-node="8\,2\,0" data-
 index-in-node="90">January 11 – May 7</strong> residency dates.  </li><l
 i data-path-to-node="8\,0\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="8\,3\,0" data-ind
 ex-in-node="0">Logistics Bridge:</strong> Understand how the <strong data-
 path-to-node="8\,3\,0" data-index-in-node="41">IU Capital Campus</strong> 
 housing works and how the classes work for undergrads\, grad\, and PhD stu
 dents.  </li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node="10"><strong data-path-to-node="10
 " data-index-in-node="0">The Agenda</strong></h3><p data-path-to-node="11\
 ,0\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="11\,0\,0" data-index-in-node="0">I. The 
 Practitioner Perspective:</strong> A briefing from Ambassador Lee Feinstei
 n on D.C. professional realities and "tradecraft" skills.</p><p data-path-
 to-node="11\,1\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="11\,1\,0" data-index-in-node
 ="0">II. The Roadmap:</strong> A deep dive into the <strong data-path-to-n
 ode="11\,1\,0" data-index-in-node="38">October 15</strong> deadline\, inte
 rview sprints (Oct 26–28)\, and the mandatory December 12 orientation.</
 p><p data-path-to-node="11\,2\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="11\,2\,0" dat
 a-index-in-node="0">III. Housing &amp\; Classes:</strong> Guidance on the 
 Capital Campus residency and the academic courses offered in D.C.</p><p da
 ta-path-to-node="11\,3\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="11\,3\,0" data-index
 -in-node="0">IV. Ground Game:</strong> Peer-to-peer breakouts and alumni p
 anel discussion on commuting\, and professional life in DC.</p><p class="i
 ntro" data-path-to-node="14"><strong>Can't make the full hour? No problem.
  This is a come-and-go strategy session designed to fit your Thursday sche
 dule.</strong></p><p class="intro" data-path-to-node="14"><strong>Link to 
 Application: <a class="external" href="https://iu.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/fo
 rm/SV_bxucZoEtLdi24aW">https://iu.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_bxucZoEtLd
 i24a</a></strong></p><h3 data-path-to-node="13"><strong data-path-to-node=
 "13" data-index-in-node="0">______________________________________________
 __________</strong></h3><h3 data-path-to-node="13"><strong data-path-to-no
 de="13" data-index-in-node="0">Biography: Ambassador &amp\; Professor Lee 
 Feinstein</strong></h3><p class="intro" data-path-to-node="14">  Ambassado
 r Lee Feinstein is a Senior Managing Director and the President of McLarty
  Associates. He previously served as the U.S. Ambassador to the Republic o
 f Poland and held senior positions at the Department of State\, including 
 Principal Deputy Director and a Member of the Policy Planning Staff. He wa
 s the Founding Dean of the Hamilton Lugar School of Global and Internation
 al Studies at Indiana University from 2014 to 2022. Ambassador Feinstein i
 s a member of the Council on Foreign Relations and the American Academy of
  Diplomacy\, and holds a JD from Georgetown University Law Center.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<div>\n  <strong data-olk-copy-source="MailCompos
 e">Katherine A. Ntiamoah<br />\n  kntiamoa@iu.edu</strong>\n</div>\n<div>\
 n  Director of Policy Engagement and Strategic Partnerships\n</div>\n<div>
 \n  Hamilton Lugar School of Global &amp\; International Studies\n</div>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2344613
X-LIVEWHALE-RSVP:1
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  <strong data-path-to-node="5" data-index-in-nod
 e="281">Join Academic Director &amp\; Ambassador Lee Feinstein for a worki
 ng dinner on the Spring 2027 D.C. residency. Map your path to the Oct 15 d
 eadline and gain professional insights.&#160\;</strong>\n</p>
