CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Culture and languages
DESCRIPTION:Kennedy prints beautiful posters with famous quotes\, motivati
 onal and provocative messages\, and event advertisements by using colorful
  layers of text. His technique is also present in his books\, where he use
 s quotes in conjunction with textiles\, images\, and colorful paper to exp
 lore literary works\, social injustices against Black Americans\, and Afri
 can proverbs and riddles. &#160\;  Feel free to drop in as your schedule p
 ermits!&#160\;
GEO:39.171003;-86.516793
LAST-MODIFIED:20260818T172952Z
LOCATION:HERMAN B WELLS LIBRARY
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2375553-refusing-to-rest-the-books-a
 nd-prints-of-amos-paul
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Kennedy prints beautiful posters with fa
 mous quotes\, motivational and provocative messages\, and event advertisem
 ents by using colorful layers of text. His technique is also present in hi
 s books\, where he uses quotes in conjunction with textiles\, images\, and
  colorful paper to explore literary works\, social injustices against Blac
 k Americans\, and African proverbs and riddles. &#160\;</p><p>  Feel free 
 to drop in as your schedule permits!&#160\;</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>Sarah Carter\, Art\, Architecture\, and Design
  Librarian\, <a href="mailto:saccarte@iu.edu">saccarte@iu.edu</a>&#160\;</
 p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2385085
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>Pop-up exhibition of work by Amos Paul Kennedy Jr.\
 , a printmaker who uses his press to bring printing back to Black culture 
 and "put messages in the hands of the people"\, as he says.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TAGS:Arts and Humanities
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:Architecture + Design, IU Arts & Humanities Institute, IU Bloomington Libraries, IU Eskenazi School of Art
END:VEVENT
