X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_261
SUMMARY:Publishing Your Research: Know Your OAptions and Copyrights
DTSTART:20260921T180000Z
DTEND:20260921T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260729T144942Z
UID:20260921T180000Z-2364522@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260921T180000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1920,1920/31615_fall_into_research_livewhale_avatar.rev.1
 785270700.jpg
CATEGORIES:Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Join the Head of the Copyright Program and the Director of Sch
 olarly Communication and Open Publishing for an overview of how copyright 
 and publishing choices can affect the visibility\, reuse\, and long-term i
 mpact of your work. We will debunk common copyright myths that can inadver
 tently limit the reach of your scholarship and explore practical strategie
 s for increasing research impact through ORCID and IUScholarWorks. Whether
  you are preparing your first article or looking to expand the reach of an
  established research portfolio\, this workshop will help you make informe
 d decisions about sharing and preserving your scholarship.__________  New 
 to research\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in learning mo
 re about research data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 sem
 ester\, join us for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of re
 searching with data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to meet
 ing funder requirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Librari
 es\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessi
 ons useful for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require advance
 d registration.  For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Resea
 rch Data Services team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don'
 t forget to check back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260811T230918Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2364522-publishing-your-research
 -know-your-oaptions-and-copy
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="none">Join the Head o
 f the Copyright Program and the Director of Scholarly Communication and Op
 en Publishing for an overview of how copyright and publishing choices can 
 affect the visibility\, reuse\, and long-term impact of your work. We will
  debunk common copyright myths that can inadvertently limit the reach of y
 our scholarship and explore practical strategies for increasing research i
 mpact through ORCID and IUScholarWorks. Whether you are preparing your fir
 st article or looking to expand the reach of an established research portf
 olio\, this workshop will help you make informed decisions about sharing a
 nd preserving your scholarship.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;134233
 117&quot\;:false\,&quot\;134233118&quot\;:false\,&quot\;335559738&quot\;:2
 40\,&quot\;335559739&quot\;:0}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="none">_
 _________</span></p><p>  New to research\, new to managing your own data\,
  or interested in learning more about research data support at IU? Over th
 e course of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to walk
  you through the basics of researching with data at IU— from organizing 
 and storing your data to meeting funder requirements and finding the right
  tools.</p><p>  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, an
 d other campus partners\, with sessions useful for researchers at any stag
 e. Some sessions may require advanced registration.</p><p>  For any questi
 ons\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Services team (<a href
 ="mailto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>) - and don't forget to check b
 ack regularly\, as new sessions are added!</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  IU Libraries Research Data Services: <a hr
 ef="mailto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>&#160\;\n</p>
