 icture></strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p>          &#160\;        </p>
 </td></tr><tr><td colspan="2"><p style="text-align: center\;">          &#
 160\;        </p><p style="text-align: center\;"><strong><em>By Their Own 
 Hands: The Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame!</em></strong></p><p>          Fo
 unded in 1974 by the Culture and Ethnic Affairs Guild of the Oakland Museu
 m of California\, the Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame began as a film lectur
 e series and awards ceremony celebrating achievements of Black film indust
 ry figures. When that organization closed\, they donated their materials t
 o IU. In collaboration with the IU Black Film Center and Archive\, this ex
 hibit features objects from that collection\, including founding documents
 \, costumes\, and handprints of inductees to the Hall of Fame.        </p>
 <p style="text-align: center\;"><strong>Dates: September 2025 - December 2
 026</strong></p><p>          &#160\;        </p><picture class="lw_image l
 w_image28163  lw_align_center"><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://e
 vents.iu.edu/live/image/gid/479/width/250/height/125/28163_27301_3_handpri
 nts.rev.1758043255.webp 1x" data-origin="responsive"/><source type="image/
