DESCRIPTION:This MAP Session is the first session of the year. Help improv
 e your goal-setting skills and set some actionable goals for the year ahe
 ad!\nThe Mentor Apprenticeship Program (MAP) is a two-semester training s
 eries facilitated by the FASE Mentoring Program. It gives students at IU 
 Bloomington opportunities to enhance their mentoring\, teamwork\, and lea
 dership skills. Upon completion of MAP\, students receive a Certificate o
 f Completion\, which establishes their commitment to growth and leadershi
 p.\nAll Indiana University events\, groups\, activities\, educational\, c
 ultural\, and historical observances welcome all IU students and other me
 mbers of the Indiana University community.\n\nHosted by: Mentoring Servic
 es and Leadership Development \n\nAdditional Information can be found at:
  https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12517604
