CATEGORIES:Career development
DESCRIPTION:Join William E. Padgett\, Partner (Maurer '94)\, and Kathleen 
 Waak (Maurer '20)\, Associate\, at Barnes &amp\; Thornburg for a discussio
 n on "The Intersections of Science\, Law\, and Opportunities in Litigation
 ."  Padgett and Waak practice in Barnes &amp\; Thornburg's Drug\, Device a
 nd Consumer Products (DDCP) and Product Liability and Mass Torts (PLMT) pr
 actice groups. These nationally recognized groups are the largest practice
  groups at the 800+ attorney firm. Drawing on their work at Barnes &amp\; 
 Thornburg\, they will share how science and law intersect in their litigat
 ion practices and introduce students to opportunities in these areas of pr
 actice.  No background in science is necessary. All Maurer students are we
 lcome and encouraged to attend.
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
LAST-MODIFIED:20260903T214355Z
LOCATION:Lowell E. Baier Hall - DeLaney Moot Court Room - 123
