 r '94)\, and Kathleen Waak (Maurer '20)\, Associate\, at Barnes &amp\; Tho
 rnburg for a discussion on "The Intersections of Science\, Law\, and Oppor
 tunities in Litigation."</p><p>  Padgett and Waak practice in Barnes &amp\
 ; Thornburg's Drug\, Device and Consumer Products (DDCP) and Product Liabi
 lity and Mass Torts (PLMT) practice groups. These nationally recognized gr
 oups are the largest practice groups at the 800+ attorney firm. Drawing on
  their work at Barnes &amp\; Thornburg\, they will share how science and l
 aw intersect in their litigation practices and introduce students to oppor
 tunities in these areas of practice.</p><p>  No background in science is n
 ecessary. All Maurer students are welcome and encouraged to attend.</p>
