END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_bloomington_in_gov_1rosks8nont4ebaq41tfgg8v7g_group_calendar_google_com
SUMMARY:Parks for Pollinators BioBlitz
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260923T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260923T180000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041602Z
UID:70ok685ogo6fapuhg0labolqh8@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260923T163000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260827T125225Z
DESCRIPTION:<h2>Parks for Pollinators BioBlitz</h2><p>Parks and Recreation
  has a goal to collect both pollinator AND plant observations from every c
 ity park during the National Parks and Recreation Association's annual Par
 ks for Pollinators BioBlitz! </p><p>To participate\, get the free iNatura
 list app on your phone\, and <a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/projects
 /parks-for-pollinators-2026-bloomington-in-parks-and-rec-bee-city-blooming
 ton">join the BioBlitz hosted by Bloomington Bee City.</a> Visit any-or al
 l!-city parks between Sept. 1 and Sept. 30 and take clear photos of bees\,
  butterflies\, flowers\, and other wildlife. Submit your observations thro
 ugh the iNaturalist app to add data to the national count!</p><ul><li><a h
 ref="https://volunteer.bloomington.in.gov/acts/console.php?console_id=0286
 &amp\;console_type=event&amp\;cat_id=16&amp\;ht=1">Volunteer for the Polli
 nator Garden Maintenance Day</a> Sept. 19 at Park Ridge East Park to parti
 cipate in the BioBlitz and learn about plant and pollinator identification
  with Parks and Recreation staff.</li><li><a href="https://cerv.is/0286x12
 46">Register now for a BioBlitz event.</a> Attend one or all for hands-on 
 instructions and more information about supporting pollinators in City par
 ks.<ul><li>Sept. 21 from 12-1:30 p.m. at Switchyard Park (meet at the Comm
 unity Foundation Switchyard Plaza Spray Pad)</li><li>Sept. 23 from 4:30-6 
 p.m. at Rogers Family Park\, meet at the barn</li><li>Sept. 24 from 1-2:30
  p.m. at Crestmont Park\, meet at the 13th Street parking lot</li><li>Sept
 . 25 from 2:30-4 p.m. at Miller-Showers Park\, meet at the waterfall off 1
 7th Street</li></ul></li></ul>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260827T125225Z
LOCATION:Rogers Family Park\, 2000 E Winslow Rd\, Bloomington\, IN 47401\,
  USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Parks and Recreation
END:VEVENT
