BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Browncounty": "https://browncounty.com/events/the-fixx-colin-blunstone-the-voice-of-the-zombies-peter-asher/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:browncounty
SUMMARY:The FIXX\, Colin Blunstone (The Voice of The Zombies) & Peter Ashe
 r
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260923T230000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260923T230000
DTSTAMP:20260625T151606Z
UID:MEC-3a41d6c90db7829c7dedd2419cd59b7d@browncounty.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260923T230000
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 06/2-scaled.jpeg
CATEGORIES:Entertainment,Happening,Live Music
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260625
DESCRIPTION:The British are coming… back! Multi-platinum rockers The FIX
 X\, Colin Blunstone (the legendary voice of The Zombies) and Peter Asher (
 of Peter & Gordon)\, join forces for a remarkable night of Brit-rock that 
 transcends generations. The show will make a stop at the Brown County Musi
 c Center in Nashville\, Ind.\, on Wednesday\, September 23\, 2026.\nThe FI
 XX has been often heralded as one of the most innovative bands to come out
  of the MTV era. Instantly recognizable\, The FIXX sound is unmistakably u
 nique and stands out among the thousands of artists filling the airwaves. 
 Songs such as “One Thing Leads To Another\,” “Red Skies” and “Sa
 ved By Zero” remain everyday staples in television\, films and on radio 
 stations that continue to break new acts inspired by the era that The FIXX
  helped to define. The FIXX (were then and still are now): Cy Curnin on vo
 cals\, Rupert Greenall on keyboards\, Jamie West-Oram on guitar\, Adam Woo
 ds on drums\, and bassist Dan K. Brown.\nColin Blunstone\, lead singer of 
 The Zombies and acclaimed solo artist\, returns to U.S. stages this autumn
  alongside The FIXX and Peter Asher. His career-spanning show will feature
  classics from The Zombies\, favourites from his solo releases and collabo
 rations. The world first fell in love with that mysteriously silky voice f
 rom The Zombies’ 1960’s singles “She’s Not There\,” “Tell Her 
 No\,” and “Time of the Season.” The band’s untimely demise in late
  1967 led Blunstone into a solo career which began in earnest with the rel
 ease of the lush and string-laden One Year in 1971\, produced by former Zo
 mbies’ bandmates Rod Argent and Chris White\, which scored him a Top 15 
 UK hit with Denny Laine’s “Say You Don’t Mind.” He has released 10
  albums of his own over a period spanning more than 50 years\, including 1
 972’s Ennismore and 1974’s Journey\, and has lent his remarkable pipes
  to the recordings of many others\, most notably the Alan Parsons Project\
 , who featured Blunstone on their 1982 hit “Old and Wise\,” as well as
  on several albums. Blunstone celebrated his 80th birthday at the London p
 remiere of Hung Up On A Dream: The Zombies Documentary\, the first-ever fe
 ature film chronicling the band’s journey from teenage friends to Rock &
  Roll Hall of Fame Inductees (now available on AppleTV and Amazon). With A
 rgent’s retirement for health reasons in 2024\, Blunstone is refocusing 
 on his solo career while also continuing to celebrate the legacy of The Zo
 mbies. A new album\, produced by George Moore\, is planned for release in 
 2027.\nWe first came to know Peter Asher through the Lennon/McCartney-penn
 ed global smash “World Without Love” as one half of the British Invasi
 on duo Peter & Gordon\, whose 10 Top 40 hits (“Lady Godiva\,” “I Go 
 To Pieces\,” Lennon/McCartney’s “Woman\,” “I Don’t to See You 
 Again\,” etc) cemented them in our collective consciousness. But Peter A
 sher ultimately became a legend in the entertainment world as an A & R exe
 cutive for the Beatles’ Apple Records\, and as manager and/or producer o
 f the likes of James Taylor\, Linda Ronstadt\, Carole King\, Joni Mitchell
 \, Diana Ross\, Cher\, Neil Diamond\, Morrissey\, Roger Waters and so many
  more. His work reached incredible heights of both success and creativity\
 , landing him on the cover of Rolling Stone in the ‘70s and finally resu
 lting in a trip to Buckingham Palace as he became a Commander of the Most 
 Excellent Order of the British Empire in 2015. His work as the producer\, 
 alongside Walter Afanasieff\, of Barbra Streisand’s June 2025 release Th
 e Secret Of Life: Partners Volume 2 brought him into the studio with Ameri
 ca’s most legendary female vocalist as they worked on songs with James T
 aylor\, Paul McCartney\, Sting\, Sam Smith\, Hozier\, Mariah Carey\, Arian
 a Grande\, Laufey and more. Peter’s spellbinding storytellers-style perf
 ormance will bring to you the songs and stories that have endeared him to 
 generations of fans through his music with Peter & Gordon\, the great reco
 rdings he’s produced\, and his SiriusXM radio show\, “From Me To You\,
 ” and the book based on it\, “The Beatles From A to Zed.”\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260630
LOCATION:200 Maple Leaf Boulevard\, Nashville\, IN 47448
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/the-fixx-colin-blunstone-the-voice-of-t
 he-zombies-peter-asher/
X-SOURCE:Brown County Events
END:VEVENT
