X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Browncounty": "https://browncounty.com/events/uncle-pen-fest/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:browncounty
SUMMARY:Uncle Pen Fest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260924T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260926T220000
DTSTAMP:20260319T122339Z
UID:MEC-f59da5b52d6e11724f302e9ed5074290@browncounty.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260924T120000
SEQUENCE:1
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/
 07/BVB-Image-2017-Bill-Monroe-Music-Park-2-Edit-FNL.jpg
CATEGORIES:Entertainment,Festivals,Happening,Live Music,Outdoor Concerts
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260319
DESCRIPTION:Various bluegrass performers\, workshops\, and jams plus the B
 luegrass Hall of Fame Induction.\nFounded in 1974\, Uncle Pen Days began a
 s a tribute to Bill Monroe’s maternal uncle\, James Pendleton Vandiver. 
 “Uncle Pen” played the fiddle and Monroe later said that he was the 
 “fellow that I learned to play from.” Bill Monroe’s parents had both
  died by the time he was 16\, and Monroe lived part of the time this his u
 ncle\, where he would play mandolin while his uncle played fiddle at local
  square dances and social events.\nGreatly influenced by Vandiver\, Bill M
 onroe wrote a song about him\, Uncle Pen\, in 1950 — a song that went on
  to be a hit for Porter Wagoner (1954) and Ricky Skaggs (1984).\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260811
LOCATION:5163 North State Road 135\, Morgantown\, IN
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/uncle-pen-fest/
X-SOURCE:Brown County Events
END:VEVENT
