BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 261": "https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2354119-home-away-from-home-student-life-on-campus"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_261
SUMMARY:Home Away from Home: Student Life on Campus
DTSTART:20260924T130000Z
DTEND:20260924T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260717T152335Z
UID:20260907T130000Z-2354119@events.iu.edu__20260924
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1800,1800/31497_StudentLifeThumbnail_1.rev.1784316196.png
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:Spanning across four decades—1970s to the 2000s—items incl
 uding scrapbooks\, photographs\, student papers\, and handbooks demonstrat
 e life on and off campus. From decorating dorm rooms to chasing campus gho
 sts\, students have always found ways to build community and make new memo
 ries. This exhibit highlights the student experience and the multitude of 
 ways students found a sense of home\, identity and belonging at Indiana Un
 iversity.
GEO:39.171003;-86.516793
LAST-MODIFIED:20260717T192335Z
LOCATION:HERMAN B WELLS LIBRARY
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2354119-home-away-from-home-stud
 ent-life-on-campus
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Spanning across four decades—1970s to 
 the 2000s—items including scrapbooks\, photographs\, student papers\, an
 d handbooks demonstrate life on and off campus. From decorating dorm rooms
  to chasing campus ghosts\, students have always found ways to build commu
 nity and make new memories. This exhibit highlights the student experience
  and the multitude of ways students found a sense of home\, identity and b
 elonging at Indiana University.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>University Archives\, <a href="mailto:archives
 @iu.edu">archives@iu.edu</a>&#160\;</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2354119
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1800\,1800/31497_StudentLifeThumbnail_1.rev.
 1784316196.png
X-LIVEWHALE-REPEATS-UNTIL:2026-10-30 13:00:00
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>Going to college offers a variety of new freedoms\,
  excitements\, and difficulties as students make the transition away from 
 home. This exhibit features a selection of materials that represents the w
 ays first-year students made Indiana University their second home.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TAGS:exhibition|Hoosier Welcome|Indiana University Archives|IU
  History
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:IU Bloomington Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_bloomington_in_gov_1rosks8nont4ebaq41tfgg8v7g_group_calendar_google_com
SUMMARY:Parks for Pollinators BioBlitz
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260924T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260924T143000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041602Z
UID:5hkjecit2436vdlqo28tp2j1ph@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260924T130000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260827T125257Z
DESCRIPTION:<h2>Parks for Pollinators BioBlitz</h2><p>Parks and Recreation
  has a goal to collect both pollinator AND plant observations from every c
 ity park during the National Parks and Recreation Association's annual Par
 ks for Pollinators BioBlitz! </p><p>To participate\, get the free iNatura
 list app on your phone\, and <a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/projects
 /parks-for-pollinators-2026-bloomington-in-parks-and-rec-bee-city-blooming
 ton">join the BioBlitz hosted by Bloomington Bee City.</a> Visit any-or al
 l!-city parks between Sept. 1 and Sept. 30 and take clear photos of bees\,
  butterflies\, flowers\, and other wildlife. Submit your observations thro
 ugh the iNaturalist app to add data to the national count!</p><ul><li><a h
 ref="https://volunteer.bloomington.in.gov/acts/console.php?console_id=0286
 &amp\;console_type=event&amp\;cat_id=16&amp\;ht=1">Volunteer for the Polli
 nator Garden Maintenance Day</a> Sept. 19 at Park Ridge East Park to parti
 cipate in the BioBlitz and learn about plant and pollinator identification
  with Parks and Recreation staff.</li><li><a href="https://cerv.is/0286x12
 46">Register now for a BioBlitz event.</a> Attend one or all for hands-on 
 instructions and more information about supporting pollinators in City par
 ks.<ul><li>Sept. 21 from 12-1:30 p.m. at Switchyard Park (meet at the Comm
 unity Foundation Switchyard Plaza Spray Pad)</li><li>Sept. 23 from 4:30-6 
 p.m. at Rogers Family Park\, meet at the barn</li><li>Sept. 24 from 1-2:30
  p.m. at Crestmont Park\, meet at the 13th Street parking lot</li><li>Sept
 . 25 from 2:30-4 p.m. at Miller-Showers Park\, meet at the waterfall off 1
 7th Street</li></ul></li></ul>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260827T125258Z
LOCATION:Crestmont Park\, 1001 W 16th St\, Bloomington\, IN 47404\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Parks and Recreation
END:VEVENT
