X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 261": "https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2388184-lecture-the-declaration-in-a-time-of-crisis"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_261
SUMMARY:Lecture: The Declaration in a Time of Crisis
DTSTART:20260924T203000Z
DTEND:20260924T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260820T140655Z
UID:20260924T203000Z-2388184@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260924T203000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,512,512/32113_signers_event_square_web_image.rev.17872483
 09.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences
DESCRIPTION:We welcome IU Associate Professor of History Konstantin Dierks
  (https://history.indiana.edu/faculty_staff/faculty/dierks_konstantin.html
 )\, who will give a lecture entitled "The Declaration in a Time of Crisis.
 " How do people meet the moment in times of political crisis? The Declarat
 ion of Independence tried to meet the crisis of 1776. It pinned blame on K
 ing George III. It inspired enough colonists to rebel against a mighty emp
 ire. It put enduring ideals into American history. The Declaration managed
  to do so surrounded by a crisis—and before a future—far beyond its gr
 asp. How might we think\, then\, of the issues we face in 2026?  Prof. Die
 rks' talk will be followed by a reception with exhibition curators and sea
 sonal refreshments. Our friends at the Eskenazi Museum of Art will be open
  during this time for interpretive viewings of a Gilbert Stuart portrait o
 f George Washington.  Due to space limitations\, we ask attendees to RSVP 
 for this event.  Event Schedule4:30 p.m.: Konstantin Dierks | Lilly Librar
 y Lecture Hall  5:30–6:30 p.m.: Reception | Slocum Room and Lilly Librar
 y galleries  5–7 p.m.: Washington portrait viewing | Eskenazi Museum    
 For more information about visiting the Lilly Library\, including parking 
 and accessibility\, please visit the Lilly Library website (https://librar
 ies.indiana.edu/signers-opening).
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
LAST-MODIFIED:20260902T142422Z
LOCATION:LILLY LIBRARY
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2388184-lecture-the-declaration-
 in-a-time-of-crisis
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  We welcome IU Associate Professor of His
 tory <a href="https://history.indiana.edu/faculty_staff/faculty/dierks_kon
 stantin.html">Konstantin Dierks</a>\, who will give a lecture entitled "Th
 e Declaration in a Time of Crisis." How do people meet the moment in times
  of political crisis? The Declaration of Independence tried to meet the cr
 isis of 1776. It pinned blame on King George III. It inspired enough colon
 ists to rebel against a mighty empire. It put enduring ideals into America
 n history. The Declaration managed to do so surrounded by a crisis—and b
 efore a future—far beyond its grasp. How might we think\, then\, of the 
 issues we face in 2026?</p><p>  Prof. Dierks' talk will be followed by a r
 eception with exhibition curators and seasonal refreshments. Our friends a
 t the Eskenazi Museum of Art will be open during this time for interpretiv
 e viewings of a Gilbert Stuart portrait of George Washington.</p><p>  Due 
 to space limitations\, we ask attendees to RSVP for this event.</p><h2>  E
 vent Schedule</h2><ul><li data-list-item-id="ea0abef9d79d69c3563685c8b98a6
 a5ba">4:30 p.m.: Konstantin Dierks | Lilly Library Lecture Hall  </li><li 
 data-list-item-id="e6f7674d7d5ef9cee183419b5c1873a3e">5:30–6:30 p.m.: Re
 ception | Slocum Room and Lilly Library galleries  </li><li data-list-item
 -id="e23a7b723761f9a90fe9e9bdf3aa5919c">5–7 p.m.: Washington portrait vi
 ewing | Eskenazi Museum  </li></ul><p>  For more information about visitin
 g the Lilly Library\, including parking and accessibility\, please visit <
 a href="https://libraries.indiana.edu/signers-opening" target="_blank" rel
 ="noopener">the Lilly Library website</a>.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  <strong>Lilly Library</strong><br />\n  <a
  href="mailto:liblilly@iu.edu">liblilly@iu.edu<br />\n  <br /></a>\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2388184
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,512\,512/32113_signers_event_square_web_imag
 e.rev.1787248309.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-RSVP:1
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  <strong>***Lecture seats are now</strong> <span
  style="box-sizing: border-box\; margin: 0px\; padding: 0px\;"><strong>wai
 t-list only***</strong> We</span> have more space at the reception that fo
 llows\; please come! <a href="https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/238820
 1-opening-reception-the-declaration-of-independence">RSVP here</a> so we c
 an plan for you. Add your name below to the waiting list for the lecture.\
 n</p>
