CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:IU Libraries Lilly Library is excited to present an expansion 
 of The Declaration of Independence: The Motives the Moment\, which has mov
 ed up to the North Gallery. Joining it in the South Gallery is The Signers
  (https://libraries.indiana.edu/lilly-library/the-signers)\, focusing on t
 he signatories of the nation's founding document.  As part of our opening 
 celebration\, we are hosting a reception with seasonal refreshments. Atten
 dees can peruse the receptions at their own pace. Meanwhile\, our friends 
 at the Eskenazi Museum of Art (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/) will stay o
 pen late to provide interpretive viewings of a Gilbert Stuart portrait of 
 George Washington.  Event Schedule4:30 p.m.: Konstantin Dierks lecture | L
 illy Library Lecture Hall (requires separate registration (https://events.
 iu.edu/libraries/event/2388184-lecture-the-declaration-in-a-time-of-crisis
 ))  5:30–6:30 p.m.: Reception | Slocum Room and Lilly Library galleries 
  5–7 p.m.: Washington portrait viewing | Eskenazi Museum    For more inf
 ormation about visiting the Lilly Library\, including parking and accessib
 ility\, please visit the Lilly Library website (https://libraries.indiana.
 edu/signers-opening).
LAST-MODIFIED:20260820T185002Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2388201-opening-reception-the-de
 claration-of-independence
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  IU Libraries Lilly Library is excited to
  present an expansion of <a href="https://libraries.indiana.edu/lilly-libr
 ary/declaration-independence" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>The Decla
 ration of Independence: The Motives the Moment</em>\,</a> which has moved 
 up to the North Gallery. Joining it in the South Gallery is <em><a href="h
 ttps://libraries.indiana.edu/lilly-library/the-signers">The Signers</a></e
 m>\, focusing on the signatories of the nation's founding document.</p><p>
   As part of our opening celebration\, we are hosting a reception with sea
 sonal refreshments. Attendees can peruse the receptions at their own pace.
  Meanwhile\, our friends at the <a href="https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/" t
 arget="_blank" rel="noopener">Eskenazi Museum of Art</a> will stay open la
 te to provide interpretive viewings of a Gilbert Stuart portrait of George
  Washington.</p><h2>  Event Schedule</h2><ul><li data-list-item-id="ea0abe
 f9d79d69c3563685c8b98a6a5ba">4:30 p.m.: Konstantin Dierks lecture | Lilly 
 Library Lecture Hall (<a href="https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/23881
 84-lecture-the-declaration-in-a-time-of-crisis" target="_blank" rel="noope
 ner">requires separate registration</a>)  </li><li data-list-item-id="e6f7
 674d7d5ef9cee183419b5c1873a3e">5:30–6:30 p.m.: Reception | Slocum Room a
 nd Lilly Library galleries  </li><li data-list-item-id="e23a7b723761f9a90f
 e9e9bdf3aa5919c">5–7 p.m.: Washington portrait viewing | Eskenazi Museum
   </li></ul><p>  For more information about visiting the Lilly Library\, i
 ncluding parking and accessibility\, please visit <a class="external" href
 ="https://libraries.indiana.edu/signers-opening" target="_blank" rel="noop
 ener">the Lilly Library website</a>.</p>
