X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_261
SUMMARY:You (probably) Haven't Seen This Before - Working Joy
DTSTART:20260924T213000Z
DTEND:20260924T223000Z
DTSTAMP:20260902T132311Z
UID:20260924T213000Z-2405044@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260924T213000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,800,800/32329_Sept2026SRogers_headshot_cropped.rev.178836
 9875.png
CATEGORIES:Performances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:Dive deep into the archival collections of IU Libraries throug
 h a screening series of rare and unique archival films that center traditi
 onally underrepresented narratives and underrepresented motion-picture pra
 ctices\, pushing on and expanding the spectrum of what is considered "cine
 ma."  In an effort to keep audiences open-minded and with limited pre-conc
 eptions of these rare works of celluloid\, descriptions of films to be sho
 wn will not be shared prior to screenings. Join us based on announced them
 es and the expectation that the works you see will fall outside of Hollywo
 od tropes\, outside of mainstream commercial expectations\, and outside of
  conventional filmmaking practices. Trust us\, you (probably) haven't seen
  these films before!September Program: Working Joy\, curated by Addison Ro
 gersProgram Description: Working Joy is a concept of taking the necessary 
 break\, the leisure to help get the work done. It's also the necessary wor
 k of facilitating good times\, experiences\, true beauty. Selections from 
 IULMIA will take us through the process of enjoying life. Going through th
 e past\, we can see this has always been a practice\, and fortunately has 
 not gotten by unnoticed.Curator Bio: Addison Rogers is a prominent multi-d
 isciplinary artist\, musician\, and community fixture based in Bloomington
 \, Indiana. Best known as the drummer and co-vocalist for the acclaimed in
 die-folk outfit Busman's Holiday\, Rogers has spent over two decades shapi
 ng the local cultural landscape. From the band's early days busking on the
  B-Line Trail to recording sweeping orchestral albums for Indiana's Joyful
  Noise Recordings\, his creative career is rooted in a deep love for colla
 borative\, community-driven storytelling. Beyond his work on stage\, Roger
 s is a champion of local independent media and arts\, currently serving on
  the Board of Directors for Bloomington's community radio station\, WFHB.P
 lease register below! Advance registration is strongly encouraged and deep
 ly appreciated!
GEO:39.171006;-86.5168
LAST-MODIFIED:20260902T174253Z
LOCATION:Wells Library Screening Room 048
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2405044-you-probably-havent-seen
 -this-before-working-joy
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Dive deep into the archival collections 
 of IU Libraries through a screening series of rare and unique archival fil
 ms that center traditionally underrepresented narratives and underrepresen
 ted motion-picture practices\, pushing on and expanding the spectrum of wh
 at is considered "cinema."</p><p>  In an effort to keep audiences open-min
 ded and with limited pre-conceptions of these rare works of celluloid\, de
 scriptions of films to be shown will not be shared prior to screenings. Jo
 in us based on announced themes and the expectation that the works you see
  will fall outside of Hollywood tropes\, outside of mainstream commercial 
 expectations\, and outside of conventional filmmaking practices. Trust us\
 , you (probably) haven't seen these films before!</p><p><strong>September 
 Program</strong>: Working Joy\, curated by Addison Rogers</p><p><strong>Pr
 ogram Description</strong>: Working Joy is a concept of taking the necessa
 ry break\, the leisure to help get the work done. It's also the necessary 
 work of facilitating good times\, experiences\, true beauty. Selections fr
 om IULMIA will take us through the process of enjoying life. Going through
  the past\, we can see this has always been a practice\, and fortunately h
 as not gotten by unnoticed.</p><p><strong>Curator Bio</strong>: Addison Ro
 gers is a prominent multi-disciplinary artist\, musician\, and community f
 ixture based in Bloomington\, Indiana. Best known as the drummer and co-vo
 calist for the acclaimed indie-folk outfit Busman's Holiday\, Rogers has s
 pent over two decades shaping the local cultural landscape. From the band'
 s early days busking on the B-Line Trail to recording sweeping orchestral 
 albums for Indiana's Joyful Noise Recordings\, his creative career is root
 ed in a deep love for collaborative\, community-driven storytelling. Beyon
 d his work on stage\, Rogers is a champion of local independent media and 
 arts\, currently serving on the Board of Directors for Bloomington's commu
 nity radio station\, WFHB.</p><p><strong>Please register below! Advance re
 gistration is strongly encouraged and deeply appreciated!</strong></p><p><
 br style="font-weight: 400\;" /><br style="font-weight: 400\;" /></p>
