SUMMARY:Developing a Secure and Private Research Roadmap from Project Idea
  to Data Destruction
DTSTART:20260929T170000Z
DTEND:20260929T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20260729T145638Z
UID:20260929T170000Z-2364524@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260929T170000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1920,1920/31615_fall_into_research_livewhale_avatar.rev.1
 785270700.jpg
CATEGORIES:Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:This session introduces SecureMyFutureResearch\, a course desi
 gned to help graduate-level researchers anticipate these requirements befo
 re they create delays\, uncertainty\, or risks to research data. Participa
 nts will receive an overview of the course's six-stage research lifecycle 
 roadmap\, from developing a project and obtaining approvals through data c
 ollection\, retention\, sharing\, and destruction.__________  New to resea
 rch\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in learning more about
  research data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, 
 join us for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of researchin
 g with data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to meeting fund
 er requirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the
  IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions usef
 ul for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require advanced regist
 ration.  For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data
  Services team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don't forget
  to check back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260811T225300Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2364524-developing-a-secure-and-
 private-research-roadmap-fro
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="none">This session in
 troduces SecureMyFutureResearch\, a course designed to help graduate-level
  researchers anticipate these requirements before they create delays\, unc
 ertainty\, or risks to research data. Participants will receive an overvie
 w of the course's six-stage research lifecycle roadmap\, from developing a
  project and obtaining approvals through data collection\, retention\, sha
 ring\, and destruction.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;134233117&quot
 \;:false\,&quot\;134233118&quot\;:false\,&quot\;335559738&quot\;:240\,&quo
 t\;335559739&quot\;:0}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="none">_________
 _</span></p><p>  New to research\, new to managing your own data\, or inte
 rested in learning more about research data support at IU? Over the course
  of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to walk you thr
 ough the basics of researching with data at IU— from organizing and stor
 ing your data to meeting funder requirements and finding the right tools.<
 /p><p>  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other 
 campus partners\, with sessions useful for researchers at any stage. Some 
 sessions may require advanced registration.</p><p>  For any questions\, pl
 ease contact the IU Libraries Research Data Services team (<a href="mailto
 :resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>) - and don't forget to check back regu
 larly\, as new sessions are added!</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  IU Libraries Research Data Services: <a hr
 ef="mailto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>&#160\;\n</p>
