DESCRIPTION:While incredibly powerful\, it requires a significant amount o
 f time and preparation to be done well. Attendees of this webinar will lea
 rn best practices for preparing for Evidence Synthesis (which includes Sys
 tematic Reviews\, Scoping Reviews\, Umbrella Reviews\, etc.)\, and the too
 ls and support available to IU researchers.__________  New to research\, n
 ew to managing your own data\, or interested in learning more about resear
 ch data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us
  for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of researching with 
 data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to meeting funder requ
 irements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Res
 earch Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions useful for 
 researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require advanced registration.
   For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Servic
 es team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don't forget to che
 ck back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
