DESCRIPTION:Attend an exclusive working dinner and strategy session for th
 e Spring 2027 D.C. Global Policy Program. Don't just study global leadersh
 ip. Put it into practice.  This intimate event is for students interested 
 in the Hamilton Lugar Spring 2027 residency. It's a working dinner and a p
 eek at what a global career actually feels like before you step into it.Wh
 y you should attend:Sit at the Table: Engage with leaders who have shaped 
 global policy and international careers.    Alumni Insights: Hear from a p
 anel of D.C. Program alumni regarding their on-the-ground experiences.    
 Professional Roadmap: Get a technical walkthrough of the Spring 2027 cycle
 \, including the January 12 – May 2 residency dates.    The Logistics Br
 idge: Understand how the IU Capital Campus housing works and how the class
 es work for undergrads\, grad\, and PhD students.    The Strategy Session 
 AgendaI. The Practitioner Perspective: A briefing from Ambassador Lee Fein
 stein on D.C. professional realities and "tradecraft" skills.    II. The R
 oadmap: A deep dive into the October 15 deadline\, interview sprints (Oct 
 26–28)\, and the mandatory December 12 orientation.    III. Housing &amp
 \; Classes: Guidance on the Capital Campus residency and the academic cour
 ses offered in D.C.    IV. Ground Game: Peer-to-peer breakouts and alumni 
 panel discussion on commuting\, and professional life in DC.    Biography:
  Ambassador &amp\; Professor Lee Feinstein  Ambassador Lee Feinstein is a 
 Senior Managing Director and the President of McLarty Associates. He previ
 ously served as the U.S. Ambassador to the Republic of Poland and held sen
 ior positions at the Department of State\, including Principal Deputy Dire
 ctor and a Member of the Policy Planning Staff. He was the Founding Dean o
 f the Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International Studies at Indiana
  University from 2014 to 2022. Ambassador Feinstein is a member of the Cou
 ncil on Foreign Relations and the American Academy of Diplomacy\, and hold
 s a JD from Georgetown University Law Center.  &#160\;Can't make the full 
 hour? No problem. This is a come-and-go strategy session designed to fit y
 our Thursday schedule.Link to Application:https://iu.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe
 /form/SV_bxucZoEtLdi24a (https://iu.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_bxucZoEt
 Ldi24aW)
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20260812T200752Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2296373-your-dc-moment-dinner-with-a
 mbassador-and
