 1/src_region/0,0,1200,1200/32098_WEBSITE__SOCIAL_SQUARE.rev.1787237006.png
DESCRIPTION:Edgar Gomezis a queer NicaRican writer born and raised in Flor
 ida. He is the author of the memoirs High-Risk Homosexual (Soft Skull Pres
 s\, 2022) and Alligator Tears (Crown\, 2025). For his writing he has recei
 ved the American Book Award\, a Stonewall Israel-Fishman Nonfiction Book H
 onor Award\, a Florida Book Award\, and the Lambda Literary Award.  His 
 work has been supported by The New York Foundation for the Arts\, The Nati
 onal Endowment for the Arts\, and The Black Mountain Institute. A graduate
  of the University of California's MFA program\, Gomez has written for The
  LA Times\, Poets &amp\; Writers\, Lithub\, New York Magazine\, and beyond
 . He lives between New York and Puerto Rico.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260828T192012Z
LOCATION:Morgenstern Books
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2387957-edgar-gomez-book-reading-and
 -signing
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong><span data-contrast="none">Edgar G
 omez</span></strong><span data-contrast="none">is a queer NicaRican writer
  born and raised in Florida. He is the author of the memoirs High-Risk Hom
 osexual (Soft Skull Press\, 2022) and Alligator Tears (Crown\, 2025). For 
 his writing he has received the American Book Award\, a Stonewall Israel-F
 ishman Nonfiction Book Honor Award\, a Florida Book Award\, and the Lambda
  Literary Award.  His work has been supported by The New York Foundation
  for the Arts\, The National Endowment for the Arts\, and The Black Mounta
 in Institute. A graduate of the University of California's MFA program\, G
 omez has written for The LA Times\, Poets &amp\; Writers\, Lithub\, New Yo
 rk Magazine\, and beyond. He lives between New York and Puerto Rico.</span
 ><span data-ccp-props="{}"></span></p>
