X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_261
SUMMARY:Home Away from Home: Student Life on Campus
DTSTART:20261002T130000Z
DTEND:20261002T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260717T152335Z
UID:20260907T130000Z-2354119@events.iu.edu__20261002
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1800,1800/31497_StudentLifeThumbnail_1.rev.1784316196.png
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:Spanning across four decades—1970s to the 2000s—items incl
 uding scrapbooks\, photographs\, student papers\, and handbooks demonstrat
 e life on and off campus. From decorating dorm rooms to chasing campus gho
 sts\, students have always found ways to build community and make new memo
 ries. This exhibit highlights the student experience and the multitude of 
 ways students found a sense of home\, identity and belonging at Indiana Un
 iversity.
GEO:39.171003;-86.516793
LAST-MODIFIED:20260717T192335Z
LOCATION:HERMAN B WELLS LIBRARY
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2354119-home-away-from-home-stud
 ent-life-on-campus
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Spanning across four decades—1970s to 
 the 2000s—items including scrapbooks\, photographs\, student papers\, an
 d handbooks demonstrate life on and off campus. From decorating dorm rooms
  to chasing campus ghosts\, students have always found ways to build commu
 nity and make new memories. This exhibit highlights the student experience
  and the multitude of ways students found a sense of home\, identity and b
 elonging at Indiana University.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>University Archives\, <a href="mailto:archives
 @iu.edu">archives@iu.edu</a>&#160\;</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2354119
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1800\,1800/31497_StudentLifeThumbnail_1.rev.
 1784316196.png
X-LIVEWHALE-REPEATS-UNTIL:2026-10-30 13:00:00
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>Going to college offers a variety of new freedoms\,
  excitements\, and difficulties as students make the transition away from 
 home. This exhibit features a selection of materials that represents the w
 ays first-year students made Indiana University their second home.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TAGS:exhibition|Hoosier Welcome|Indiana University Archives|IU
  History
