BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"BloomingtonOnline Events": "https://www.facebook.com/events/1581183743008999/", "Limestone Post": "https://www.monroehumane.org/5K"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gcal D1087E97D4Ace1C1Ca2Dd6336D417Bea870Ddac277Be6D1711Cbc0235Aa85228": "https://www.facebook.com/events/1581183743008999/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_d1087e97d4ace1c1ca2dd6336d417bea870ddac277be6d1711cbc0235aa85228
SUMMARY:31st Annual Run for the Animals 5K
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T110000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041504Z
UID:e1581183743008999@facebook.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T093000
SEQUENCE:5419592
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260306T125958Z
DESCRIPTION:Please join us on Sunday\, October 4th\, for MCHA's 31st Annua
 l Run for the Animals presented by The Dog House!\n\nLearn more & register
  at monroehumane.org/5k\n\nRun for the Animals is a timed 5K run/walk at K
 arst Farm Park\, with a portion of the course winding through the Monroe C
 ounty Fairgrounds. All of the proceeds benefit the programs and services o
 f Monroe County Humane Association.\n\nNEW in 2026\, we're introducing sep
 arate start times for runners and walkers! The course starts at Karst Farm
  Park and loops through the Monroe County Fairgrounds. The awards ceremony
  and sponsor booths are now located near the start/finish line\, making it
  easier for participants and families to celebrate together—and for fast
 er results posting! After the awards\, stick around for the raffles and fa
 n-favorite pet contests. You don't have to be registered in the 5K to part
 icipate in the raffle and pet contests!\n\nThis event is so important to M
 CHA and our ability to provide programs and services that would otherwise 
 not exist in our community\, including accessible veterinary care\, spay/n
 euter assistance\, crisis housing\, emergency pet food & supply pantry\, s
 treet outreach\, and more. MCHA is a private 501c3 non-profit that receive
 s no funding from national organizations or tax dollars. \n\nWe anticipate
  welcoming hundreds of runners\, walkers\, and canine friends to this even
 t! Don’t miss this great opportunity to support animal welfare in our co
 mmunity!\n\nEVENT SCHEDULE:\n\nSaturday\, October 3\n10:00 AM–12:00 PM &
  5:00–7:00 PM: Preregistered Packet Pick-up at Karst Farm Park Commons B
 ldg\n\nSunday\, October 4\n8:00 AM: Packet Pick-up & Onsite Registration O
 pens\n9:15 AM: Registration Closes\, Trainer-led Group Stretch\n9:30 AM: 5
 K Run Begins\n9:35 AM: 5K Walk Begins\n10:30 AM: 5K Run/Walk Awards Ceremo
 ny\n11:00 AM: Pet Contests & Raffle Winners Announced\n\n\n5K Award Catego
 ries:\n\nTop 3 Overall Men's 5K\nTop 3 Overall Women's 5K\nTop 3 Youth (12
  & under) Male 5K\nTop 3 Youth (12 & under) Female 5K\nTop Male & Top Fema
 le 13-17 years\nTop Male & Top Female 18-24 years\nTop Male & Top Female 2
 5-29 years\nTop Male & Top Female 30-39 years\nTop Male & Top Female 40-49
  years\nTop Male & Top Female 50-59 years\nTop Male & Top Female 60+ years
 \nTop 3 Canine 5K\n\nImportant Notice for Canine Participants: As required
  by the state of Indiana\, all dogs must be up to date on the rabies vacci
 nation. In addition\, only spayed/neutered dogs are permitted to participa
 te. (Visit monroehumane.org for information on Spay/Neuter Assistance.) Al
 l dogs must remain on a leash at all times during the event. For safety re
 asons\, retractable leashes are not permitted—only standard\, non-retrac
 table leashes are allowed. Thank you for helping us ensure a safe and fun 
 event for everyone!\n\n👏👏👏 THANK YOU TO OUR SPONSORS:\n\nPRESENTI
 NG SPONSOR: The 31st Annual Run for the Animals is presented by The Dog Ho
 use\, offering cage-free boarding in a cozy\, home-like environment. With 
 24-hour staffing and personalized care\, The Dog House strives to be your 
 pet’s home away from home. Learn more at trydoghouse.com.\n\nGOLD SPONSO
 RS: Monroe County Parks and Recreation & Monroe County Fairgrounds\nSILVER
  SPONSORS: BloomingPaws\; German American Bank\; & Slotegraaf Niehoff P.C.
 \nBRONZE SPONSORS: IU Credit Union & Smithville\n\nhttps://www.facebook.co
 m/events/1581183743008999/
LAST-MODIFIED:20260306T130000Z
LOCATION:Karst Farm Park
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1581183743008999/
X-SOURCE:BloomingtonOnline Events, Limestone Post
END:VEVENT
