DESCRIPTION:We'll discuss everything from file organization and naming con
 ventions to writing documentation that future users will understand. We'll
 cover choosingappropriate fileformats\, creating a data dictionary or code
 book\, and handling common issues like de-identification and missing data 
 notes. Participants will leave with a checklist they can apply to their ow
 n data beforesubmittingto a repository.__________  New to research\, new t
 o managing your own data\, or interested in learning more about research d
 ata support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for
  webinars designed to walk you through the basics of researching with data
  at IU— from organizing and storing your data to meeting funder requirem
 ents and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Researc
 h Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions useful for rese
 archers at any stage. Some sessions may require advanced registration.  Fo
 r any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Services t
 eam (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don't forget to check b
 ack regularly\, as new sessions are added!
