SUMMARY:IU Data Storage 101
DTSTART:20261006T160000Z
DTEND:20261006T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260901T170833Z
UID:20261006T160000Z-2403808@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261006T160000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1920,1920/31615_fall_into_research_livewhale_avatar.rev.1
 785270700.jpg
CATEGORIES:Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Attendees of this webinar will learn more about the various op
 tions for digital storage available through UITS Research Technologies\, i
 ncluding Slate\, Geode\, and the Scholarly Data Archive (SDA). All digital
  storage options are not made equal\, and all have various benefits and tr
 adeoffs. With this in mind\, this webinar seeks to empower users to confid
 ently make educated decisions about which types of storage work best for t
 heir particular needs and use cases.__________  New to research\, new to m
 anaging your own data\, or interested in learning more about research data
  support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for we
 binars designed to walk you through the basics of researching with data at
  IU— from organizing and storing your data to meeting funder requirement
 s and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research D
 ata Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions useful for researc
 hers at any stage. Some sessions may require advanced registration.  For a
 ny questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Services team
  (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don't forget to check back
  regularly\, as new sessions are added!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901T211237Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2403808-iu-data-storage-101
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="none">Attendees of th
 is webinar will learn more about the various options for digital storage a
 vailable through UITS Research Technologies\, including Slate\, Geode\, an
 d the Scholarly Data Archive (SDA). All digital storage options are not ma
 de equal\, and all have various benefits and tradeoffs. With this in mind\
 , this webinar seeks to empower users to confidently make educated decisio
 ns about which types of storage work best for their particular needs and u
 se cases.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;134233117&quot\;:false\,&quo
 t\;134233118&quot\;:false\,&quot\;335559738&quot\;:240\,&quot\;335559739&q
 uot\;:0}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="none">__________</span></p><p
 >  New to research\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in lear
 ning more about research data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2
 026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to walk you through the basic
 s of researching with data at IU— from organizing and storing your data 
 to meeting funder requirements and finding the right tools.</p><p>  Hosted
  by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus partner
 s\, with sessions useful for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may r
 equire advanced registration.</p><p>  For any questions\, please contact t
 he IU Libraries Research Data Services team (<a href="mailto:resdata@iu.ed
 u">resdata@iu.edu</a>) - and don't forget to check back regularly\, as new
  sessions are added!</p>
