 2.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Culture and languages,Lectures, talk
 s, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Did you know that the Eskenazi Museum actively acquires new ar
 twork each year? These works serve to engage a range of audiences and fost
 er research and learning.  Paintings\, prints\, drawings\, photographs\, a
 nd objects will be on view on the third floor in the Martha and David Moor
 e Prints\, Drawings\, and Photographs Study and the William and Diane Itte
 r Objects Study. Other newly acquired works can be explored in the gallery
  with the help of a self-guide.Drop in any time between 2 and 4 pm to see 
 the works and speak with curators who will be on hand to answer questions 
 about the pieces they acquired for the collection.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260818T172831Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2375420-new-acquisitions-open-house
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Did you know 
 that the Eskenazi Museum actively acquires new artwork each year? These wo
 rks serve to engage a range of audiences and foster research and learning.
 </p><p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Paintings\, prints\, drawings\, photog
 raphs\, and objects will be on view on the third floor in the Martha and D
 avid Moore Prints\, Drawings\, and Photographs Study and the William and D
 iane Itter Objects Study. Other newly acquired works can be explored in th
 e gallery with the help of a self-guide.</p><p style="font-weight: 400\;">
 <strong>Drop in any time between 2 and 4 pm</strong> to see the works and 
 speak with curators who will be on hand to answer questions about the piec
 es they acquired for the collection.</p>
