X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2361647-weekly-lilly-library-puzzle-tour", "IU Bloomington Libraries": "https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2361647-weekly-lilly-library-puzzle-tour"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 130": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2361647-weekly-lilly-library-puzzle-tour"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_130
SUMMARY:Weekly Lilly Library puzzle tour
DTSTART:20261009T170000Z
DTEND:20261009T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260727T114730Z
UID:20260911T170000Z-2361731@events.iu.edu__20261009
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,800,793/22582_cube_puzzle.rev.1723148057.png
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences
DESCRIPTION:Your expert guide\, our Curator of Puzzles Andrew Rhoda (https
 ://libraries.indiana.edu/andrew-rhoda)\, will introduce you to the collect
 ion\, mechanical puzzles and the collection's donor\, Jerry Slocum. You wi
 ll learn about the various categories of mechanical puzzles and their hist
 ory. You will also see highlights from the collection on exhibition in the
  Slocum Room. In addition\, there will be a group of puzzles from the coll
 ection selected by the Curator for visitors to try as part of the tour.  N
 on-flash photography is permitted\, seating is available in the Slocum Roo
 m throughout the tour\, and the building is wheelchair accessible. The tou
 r generally lasts a little less than one hour and is open to all. No reser
 vation or RSVP is required for this free tour - just drop in!
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
LAST-MODIFIED:20260727T154730Z
LOCATION:Lilly Library
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2361647-weekly-lilly-library-puzzle-
 tour
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Your expert guide\, our Curator of Puzzl
 es <a href="https://libraries.indiana.edu/andrew-rhoda">Andrew Rhoda</a>\,
  will introduce you to the collection\, mechanical puzzles and the collect
 ion's donor\, Jerry Slocum. You will learn about the various categories of
  mechanical puzzles and their history. You will also see highlights from t
 he collection on exhibition in the Slocum Room. In addition\, there will b
 e a group of puzzles from the collection selected by the Curator for visit
 ors to try as part of the tour.</p><p>  Non-flash photography is permitted
 \, seating is available in the Slocum Room throughout the tour\, and the b
 uilding is wheelchair accessible. The tour generally lasts a little less t
 han one hour and is open to all. No reservation or RSVP is required for th
 is free tour - just drop in!</p>
