DESCRIPTION:Stop by the Bloomington Community Farmers' Market to learn abo
 ut electric transportation. The newly reformed Hoosier Electric Vehicle As
 sociation will host a booth with friendly\, straightforward information ab
 out electric vehicles\, hybrids\, electric bikes\, and the practical benef
 its of more efficient and sustainable transportation.\n\nThe market runs 8
 :00 am to 12:30 pm\, with the EV booth expected to be active starting arou
 nd 9:00 am. Whether you're driving electric already\, considering your nex
 t vehicle\, or just curious how EVs fit into everyday life in Bloomington\
 , come ask questions and join the conversation. If an electric bike is on 
 hand\, it will be a good look at another side of local electric mobility.\
 n\nPart of National Drive Electric Month. A Fair of the Arts is also happe
 ning at the market this day.\n\nMore info: https://driveelectricmonth.org/
 event?eventid=5381
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T142533Z
LOCATION:Showers Commons at City Hall\, 401 N Morton Street\, Bloomington\
 , IN 47404
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:BloomingtonOnline Events, Limestone Post
END:VEVENT
