SUMMARY:Fitness in the Park: Tai Chi
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261012T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261012T200000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041602Z
UID:7m5j0hm72pkpu4ok03hv356hmk@google.com__20261012
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260814T181845Z
DESCRIPTION:<h3><b>Tai Chi in the Park</b></h3><ul><li><strong><b>Admissio
 n:</b></strong> $10 per person per class\; no pre-registration required. 
 Pay with card or cash on site.</li><li><strong><b>Day:</b></strong> Monda
 ys\, Sept. 14-Oct. 12</li><li><strong><b>Time: </b></strong>7-8 p.m.</li>
 <li><strong><b>Accessibility:</b></strong> Classes take place on the Swit
 chyard Park Main Stage. The stage is a smooth\, concrete surface accessibl
 e via ramp or stairs.</li><li><address><p>Switchyard Park\, Main Stage<br>
 1601 S. Rogers St.<br>Bloomington\, IN 47403</p></address></li></ul><p>Tai
  Chi is a moving meditation in the form of a series of gentle exercises to
  create harmony and cultivate our inner life energy (qi) to flow smoothly 
 and powerfully through the body. This is a spiritual experience\, as much 
 as a physical one.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260814T183721Z
LOCATION:Switchyard Park\, 1601 S Rogers St\, Bloomington\, IN 47403\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Parks and Recreation
END:VEVENT
