DTSTAMP:20260819T120247Z
UID:20261012T213000Z-2386389@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261012T213000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/11/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,768,959/32078_Igor_Siddiqui-headshot_by_Julie_Lacham-WEB.r
 ev.1787154985.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Siddiqui's work—manifested as objects\, images\, texts\, and
  events—links design experimentation to public engagement. He is interes
 ted in the role that interiors play in architectural experiments while adv
 ocating for experimentation in interiors as a distinct field of knowledge.
 Siddiqui's bookOblique Experiments: Claude Parent&#8217\;s Architectural I
 nstallations (1969–1975)is one of the first English-language monographs 
 on French avant-garde architect Claude Parent and the first comprehensive 
 study of his experimental interior installations from the 1970s. He recent
 ly editedInterior Experiments\, a special triple-issue ofInteriors: Design
 /Architecture/Culture\, where he has served as Editor-in-Chief\, Co-Editor
 \, and Associate Editor since 2016.His creative work has been exhibited at
  venues including the Tallinn Architecture Biennale\, Contemporary Austin\
 , SITE Santa Fe\, and Fusebox Festival\, and featured inDwell\,Interior De
 sign\,Artforum\, andTexas Architect. In 2022\, Siddiqui received the IIDA 
 Educator of the Year Award. He previously taught at the University of Penn
 sylvania\, California College of the Arts\, and Parsons. Siddiqui is a reg
 istered architect in Texas.Learn more at:https://www.igorsiddiqui.com@isss
 studio on InstagramThe Eskenazi School's Comprehensive Design and Interior
  Design programs bring renowned designers to campus for public lectures an
 d studio visits as part of the Design Speaker Series.
GEO:39.169084;-86.518997
LAST-MODIFIED:20260819T160247Z
LOCATION:Fine Arts Building\, 1201 East 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 4740
 5
URL:https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2386389-igor-siddiqui-contingent-
 communities-lecture
