CATEGORIES:Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:This session covers core de-identification techniques\, such a
 s anonymization\, aggregation\, and generalization\, along with the tradeo
 ffs between privacy protection and data utility.__________  New to researc
 h\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in learning more about r
 esearch data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, jo
 in us for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of researching 
 with data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to meeting funder
  requirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the I
 U Research Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions useful
  for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require advanced registra
 tion.  For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data S
 ervices team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don't forget t
 o check back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901T212101Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2403835-data-deidentification-in
 -compliance-with-hipaa
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span class="TextRun SCXW245376662 BCX2" l
 ang="EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="none"><span class="NormalTextR
 un SCXW245376662 BCX2">This session covers core de-identification techniqu
 es\, such as anonymization\, aggregation\, and generalization\, along with
  the tradeoffs between privacy protection and data utility.</span></span><
 /p><p><span data-contrast="none">__________</span></p><p>  New to research
 \, new to managing your own data\, or interested in learning more about re
 search data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, joi
 n us for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of researching w
 ith data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to meeting funder 
 requirements and finding the right tools.</p><p>  Hosted by IU Libraries\,
  the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions 
 useful for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require advanced re
 gistration.</p><p>  For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Re
 search Data Services team (<a href="mailto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu<
 /a>) - and don't forget to check back regularly\, as new sessions are adde
 d!</p>
