 raining, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:What Is This? Can't stay the whole time\, that is ok. This is 
 a drop-in session.&#160\;  &#160\;  No boring PowerPoint presentations. No
  passive lectures.As part of theGlobal Competencies Skills Development Ser
 ies\, this 2-hour interactive simulation drops you directly into a live hu
 manitarian crisis scenario whereyoucall the shots. You'll work in interdis
 ciplinary teams to navigate high-stakes international negotiations where c
 onflicting political interests\, limited resources\, and rapid deadlines a
 re on the line.  What You'll Get Out of It (Why You Need to Be Here)Day 1 
 Professional Tradecraft:Learn how diplomats and international crisis manag
 ers actually negotiate when peace talks stall or aid lines break.  Resume-
 Boosting Hard Skills:Gain hands-on practice inCritical Thinking\, Strategi
 c Communication\, Crisis Leadership\, and Teamwork—the top competencies 
 global employers look for.  Direct Access to a Top Senior Executive:Work s
 houlder-to-shoulder with a veteran who managed over$4 Billionin internatio
 nal humanitarian aid and led UN refugee delegations.  Open to ALL staff\, 
 students\, and faculty\, and general public:Whether you're in HLS\, O'Neil
 l\, Cybersecurity\, Data Science\, or Public Policy—undergrad or grad—
 these skills transfer directly to tech\, government\, intelligence\, and i
 nternational NGO careers.    Meet the Expert Paula Reed Lynchspent nearly 
 five decades on the front lines of U.S. foreign policy and international r
 elief. Serving 14 years in theSenior Executive Servicewithin the Departmen
 t of State's Bureau of Population\, Refugees\, and Migration (PRM)\, Paula
  oversaw budgets exceeding$4 billionfor global disaster and refugee assist
 ance.      The Highlights:    First American Rapporteur for the UN High Co
 mmissioner for Refugees (UNHCR).        Led interagency strategy across th
 e Department of State and USAID.            Helped set global standards fo
 r international refugee protection across Africa and worldwide.           
  Recipient of the Secretary of State'sCareer Achievement Award.
