BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Browncounty": "https://browncounty.com/events/author-conversation-with-kristy-woodson-harvey/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:browncounty
SUMMARY:Author Conversation with Kristy Woodson Harvey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261020T223000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261020T233000
DTSTAMP:20260803T164829Z
UID:MEC-a37ebe3beb7ae7cd94d4f54429bee90d@browncounty.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261020T223000
SEQUENCE:3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/
 11/naughtydogbooks-Instagram-3715-ig-17917344320725017.jpg
CATEGORIES:Happening,Literary,Special Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260803
DESCRIPTION:Join Naughty Dog Books in conversation with New York Times\, U
 SA Today\, and Publishers Weekly bestselling author\, Kristy Woodson Harv
 ey\, as she promotes her latest book\, Falling for Peachtree Bluff.\nTicke
 t includes:\nEntry into the event\nA signed hardback copy of Falling for P
 eachtree Bluff\n(Additional hardback copies and backlist titles will be av
 ailable for purchase at the event\, as supplies last.)\n \nDoors open 30 
 minutes before the event begins. The evening will consist of one hour of m
 oderated author conversation and Q&A\, with an optional meet-and-greet to 
 follow.\n \nAbout the book:\nWelcome to Peachtree Bluff: a cozy coastal t
 own where family secrets refuse to be washed away by the tide and close-kn
 it community is everything. As New York Times bestselling author Kristy Wo
 odson Harvey reunites the Murphy crew just in time for pumpkin spice seaso
 n\, “we dare you not to wish you were a member of this family” (E!).\n
 Eldest sister Caroline has never been happier. The family business is thri
 ving\, her kids are great\, and her sister Emerson’s hunky costar has ab
 solutely swept her off her feet. But when her not-quite-ex-husband decides
  it’s high time he begged Caroline for a second chance\, she is thrown i
 nto the midst of a love triangle she never saw coming. Caroline is the fam
 ily fixer and\, when her sisters Sloane and Emerson and daughter Vivi need
  her help with their troubles\, she has to decide whether to swoop in and 
 save them—or if it’s finally time to focus on what she wants.\nMatriar
 ch Ansley and her new husband\, Jack\, have finally hit their stride. But 
 when a scandal rips through Peachtree Bluff—and Jack just might be at th
 e center of it—Ansley is left questioning whether the man she has loved 
 since she was sixteen years old\, the man she fought so hard to be with\, 
 is actually who she thought he was at all.\nThe air is crisper\, the water
  is calmer\, but\, when it comes to the Murphy family\, nothing is ever qu
 ite as simple as it seems… Through it all\, these Southern women must re
 ly on their powerful family bonds and the quirky characters and small-town
  charm of the place that\, no matter what\, always calls them home. This i
 s the kind of heartfelt fall treat that “readers will unwrap with glee
 ” (Mary Kay Andrews\, New York Times bestselling author) from the “go-
 to for elevated beach reads” (People).\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260803
LOCATION:2359 Indiana 46 E\, Nashville\, IN
ORGANIZER;CN="Naughty Dog Books":MAILTO:
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/author-conversation-with-kristy-woodson
 -harvey/
X-SOURCE:Brown County Events
END:VEVENT
