SUMMARY:Academy of Teaching Scholars: Best Practices in Global Health Educ
 ation
DTSTART:20261028T160000Z
DTEND:20261028T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260831T153545Z
UID:20261028T160000Z-2402255@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261028T160000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/87/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,1200,800/31699_IMG_5708_1.rev.1785510945.jpg
CATEGORIES:Career development,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,T
 raining, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Global health education requires intentional curricular design
  that addresses cultural humility\, equity\, and reciprocal partnership. T
 his workshop\, presented by Dr. Jenny Baenziger\, associate director of ed
 ucation for the IU Center for Global Health\, introduces participants to e
 vidence-based approaches for preparing learners to work effectively and et
 hically in global health contexts. Special attention is given to avoiding 
 extractive educational models and centering the priorities of partner comm
 unities.Learning ObjectivesArticulate core competencies and ethical princi
 ples that should underpin global health curricula.  Evaluate global health
  educational experiences for equity\, bidirectionality\, and cultural resp
 onsiveness.  Design or revise learning objectives and preparatory activiti
 es that promote safe\, ethical\, and effective global health practice.  Th
 is event aligns with the following IUSM Academy of Teaching Scholars progr
 am competencies: Learning Theory (L) Meeting URL: https://go.iu.edu/nWrj6N
LAST-MODIFIED:20260831T193545Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2366883-academy-of-teaching-scholars
 -best-practices-in
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Global health education requires intenti
 onal curricular design that addresses cultural humility\, equity\, and rec
 iprocal partnership. This workshop\, presented by Dr. Jenny Baenziger\, as
 sociate director of education for the IU Center for Global Health\, introd
 uces participants to evidence-based approaches for preparing learners to w
 ork effectively and ethically in global health contexts. Special attention
  is given to avoiding extractive educational models and centering the prio
 rities of partner communities.</p><p><strong><em>Learning Objectives</em><
 /strong></p><ul><li>Articulate core competencies and ethical principles th
 at should underpin global health curricula.  </li><li>Evaluate global heal
 th educational experiences for equity\, bidirectionality\, and cultural re
 sponsiveness.  </li><li>Design or revise learning objectives and preparato
 ry activities that promote safe\, ethical\, and effective global health pr
 actice.  </li></ul><p><em>This event aligns with the following IUSM Academ
 y of Teaching Scholars program competencies: Learning Theory (L)</em></p> 
 Meeting URL: https://go.iu.edu/nWrj6N
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
