SUMMARY:Tommy Kha: Ghost Bites\, and Other Vietnamese Phrases | Lecture
DTSTART:20261030T210000Z
DTEND:20261030T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260902T110820Z
UID:20261030T210000Z-2404999@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261030T210000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/11/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,768,1152/32325_Tommy-Kha-photo-by-Jay_Amrahs-WEB.rev.17883
 61415.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:A 2025 Guggenheim Fellow\, Kha lives and works between New Yor
 k City and Memphis\, Tennessee\, his birthplace. He holds an M.F.A. in pho
 tography from Yale University\, where he currently teaches.Kha's work is i
 n the collections of MoMA\, SFMoMA\, George Eastman House\, the Guggenheim
  Museum\, and the Virginia Museum of Fine Arts. His first solo museum show
 \, "Other Things Uttered\," was held at the Addison Gallery of American Ar
 t in September 2025.In 2023\, Aperture published his first monograph "Half
 \, Full\, Quarter" following his solo shows "Ghost Bites" and "Má\," an o
 ngoing\, decade-long collaboration between the artist and his mother. Kha'
 s work has also appeared in The New York Times Magazine\, The New Yorker\,
  and The Wall Street Journal as well as Hyperallergic\, Interview\, McSwee
 ney's\, Vice\, Pitchfork\, Southern Cultures\, Dazed\, Foam\, Butt Magazin
 e\, and Miranda July's "We Think Alone."Kha is previously a recipient of t
 he Hayes Prize\, Next Step Award\, Foam Talent\, and NYSCA/NYFA Artist Fel
 low in Photography. He is a former resident at Pioneer Works\, Lighthouse 
 Works\, Kinosaito\, Light Work\, and BAXTER ST (née Camera Club of New Yo
 rk).He has had solo shows at Higher Pictures (which he joined in 2022)\, B
 AXTER ST\, and Blue Sky Gallery. He has taught at the New School and Rutge
 rs University and is a critic at Yale University. Currently\, Kha studies 
 kung fu under Sifu Ken Lo.According to Kha\, he "takes after his great aun
 t\, who 'read too many books and went crazy'." Artist's website:https:
 //tommykha.com (https://tommykha.com)  &#160\;
GEO:39.169084;-86.518997
LAST-MODIFIED:20260902T150820Z
LOCATION:Fine Arts Building\, 1201 East 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 4740
 5
URL:https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2404999-tommy-kha-ghost-bites-and
 -other-vietnamese-phrases
