X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2368437-global-competencies-skills-development-series-crisis", "IU Hamilton Lugar School": "https://events.iu.edu/hls/event/2368437-global-competencies-skills-development-series-crisis", "IU Kelley School of Business": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2368437-global-competencies-skills-development-series", "IU La Casa Latino Cultural Center": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2368437-global-competencies-skills-development-series-crisis"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 130": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2368437-global-competencies-skills-development-series-crisis"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_130
SUMMARY:Global Competencies Skills Development Series: Crisis\, Power & Po
 licy Dinner with Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley
DTSTART:20261103T223000Z
DTEND:20261104T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260803T144205Z
UID:20261103T223000Z-2368483@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261103T223000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/135/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,2000,2000/31509_GLOBAL_COMPETENCIES_SKILLS_DEVELOPMENT_SE
 RIES.rev.1784660853.png
CATEGORIES:Career development,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,T
 raining, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Inside the Room Where Geopolitics Happens  How do you go from 
 starting out in global affairs to shaping U.S. cyber strategy\, directing 
 counterterrorism operations\, and advising the Pentagon\, White House\, an
 d Senate?  Join the Global Competencies Skills Development Series for an i
 ntimate\, off-the-record style session with Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Wi
 nstanley—30-year Foreign Service veteran\, former U.S. Ambassador to Mal
 ta\, and President of the Middle East Policy Council.  No scripted present
 ations or generic advice—just real tradecraft from someone who has manag
 ed war-zone evacuations under fire and negotiated at the highest levels of
  national security.  Who Can Attend?  Open to all: Students (Undergrad &am
 p\; Grad)\, Faculty\, Staff\, and the Public. (Catered dinner provided)  W
 hat You'll Get Out of It      Unfiltered Access: Direct\, small-group face
  time with a senior diplomat who operated across the State Department\, De
 fense Department\, and National Security Council.          Crisis Tradecra
 ft: Real-world lessons on high-pressure decision-making\, from counterterr
 orism networks to cyber warfare and emergency evacuations.          Inside
 r Career Strategy: The exact playbook for breaking into national security\
 , intelligence\, foreign policy\, and top international fellowships.      
     Raw Answers: Bring your real questions about power dynamics\, navigati
 ng federal bureaucracy\, and building leverage early in your career.      
 Bio: Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley  Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-W
 instanley is a 30-year diplomat\, former U.S. Ambassador to the Republic o
 f Malta\, and President of the Middle East Policy Council. Her career span
 s executive leadership roles across the Department of State\, Defense Depa
 rtment\, National Security Council\, and Senate Foreign Relations Committe
 e. She has advised the commander of U.S. cyber forces on foreign policy pr
 iorities\, expanded international counterterrorism partnerships as Deputy 
 Coordinator for Counterterrorism\, and led the emergency evacuation of tho
 usands of U.S. citizens from a war zone. She is a recipient of the State D
 epartment Superior Honor Award for acts of courage during an al-Qaeda atta
 ck on the U.S. Consulate in Jeddah.
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20260810T184801Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2368437-global-competencies-skills-d
 evelopment-series-crisis
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h4 data-path-to-node="13">  Inside the Room 
 Where Geopolitics Happens</h4><p data-path-to-node="14">  How do you go fr
 om starting out in global affairs to shaping U.S. cyber strategy\, directi
 ng counterterrorism operations\, and advising the Pentagon\, White House\,
  and Senate?</p><p data-path-to-node="15">  Join the Global Competencies S
 kills Development Series for an intimate\, off-the-record style session wi
 th Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley—30-year Foreign Service vetera
 n\, former U.S. Ambassador to Malta\, and President of the Middle East Pol
 icy Council.</p><p data-path-to-node="16">  No scripted presentations or g
 eneric advice—just real tradecraft from someone who has managed war-zone
  evacuations under fire and negotiated at the highest levels of national s
 ecurity.</p><h4 data-path-to-node="17">  Who Can Attend?</h4><p data-path-
 to-node="18">  Open to all: Students (Undergrad &amp\; Grad)\, Faculty\, S
 taff\, and the Public. <i data-path-to-node="18" data-index-in-node="74">(
 Catered dinner provided)</i></p><h4 data-path-to-node="19">  What You'll G
 et Out of It</h4><ul data-path-to-node="20"><li><p data-path-to-node="20\,
 0\,0">      Unfiltered Access: Direct\, small-group face time with a senio
 r diplomat who operated across the State Department\, Defense Department\,
  and National Security Council.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="20\,
 1\,0">      Crisis Tradecraft: Real-world lessons on high-pressure decisio
 n-making\, from counterterrorism networks to cyber warfare and emergency e
 vacuations.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="20\,2\,0">      Insider 
 Career Strategy: The exact playbook for breaking into national security\, 
 intelligence\, foreign policy\, and top international fellowships.    </p>
 </li><li><p data-path-to-node="20\,3\,0">      Raw Answers: Bring your rea
 l questions about power dynamics\, navigating federal bureaucracy\, and bu
 ilding leverage early in your career.    </p></li></ul><h3 data-path-to-no
 de="22">  Bio: Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley</h3><p data-path-to-
 node="23">  Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley is a 30-year diplomat\,
  former U.S. Ambassador to the Republic of Malta\, and President of the Mi
 ddle East Policy Council. Her career spans executive leadership roles acro
 ss the Department of State\, Defense Department\, National Security Counci
 l\, and Senate Foreign Relations Committee. She has advised the commander 
 of U.S. cyber forces on foreign policy priorities\, expanded international
  counterterrorism partnerships as Deputy Coordinator for Counterterrorism\
 , and led the emergency evacuation of thousands of U.S. citizens from a wa
 r zone. She is a recipient of the State Department Superior Honor Award fo
 r acts of courage during an al-Qaeda attack on the U.S. Consulate in Jedda
 h.</p>
