X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:Michael Berryhill: good sad happy bad | Lecture
DTSTART:20261106T220000Z
DTEND:20261106T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260902T124600Z
UID:20261106T220000Z-2405020@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261106T220000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/11/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,768,768/32328_Michael-Berryhill-portrait-in-studio-CROPPED
 -WEB.rev.1788367315.jpg
DESCRIPTION:For painter Michael Berryhill\, there's no difference betw
 een realism and abstraction. His work reminds the viewer of the challenge 
 of capturing the process of painting\, and the physical and conceptual lay
 ering that a surface might contain.Berryhill has had solo exhibitions at
  Night Gallery in Los Angeles and at both Kate Werble and Derek Eller ga
 lleries in New York City and been reviewed in The New York Times\, Hyperal
 lergic\, Art in America\, Artforum\, The Brooklyn Rail\, Modern Painters\,
  Huffington Post\, Time Out NY\, Artnet News\, Flaunt magazine\,Whitehot
  Magazine of Contemporary Art\, L Magazine\, and artcritical.Berryhill e
 arned his M.F.A. from Columbia University and has held visiting faculty po
 sitions at Bard\, Columbia\, Pratt\, and VCU. Berryhill was Dean of Skow
 hegan School of Painting and Sculpture for two years. He was artist-in-res
 idence at the University of Tennessee\, Knoxville and Virginia Commonwealt
 h University in Richmond\, Virginia and held the Painting's Edge Residency
  at Idyllwild Arts Academy in California. He received a New York Foundatio
 n for the Arts Fellowship for Painting and was a Studio Space recipient 
 at the Marie Walsh Sharpe Art Foundation.Born in El Paso\, Texas\, Michael
  Berryhill earned his undergraduate degree at University of Texas Austin
 . He lives and works in Ellenville\, New York.Artist's instagram:  @berr
 yhillmichael 
GEO:39.169084;-86.518997
LAST-MODIFIED:20260902T164600Z
LOCATION:Fine Arts Building\, 1201 East 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 4740
 5
URL:https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2405020-michael-berryhill-good-sa
 d-happy-bad-lecture
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p class="p1"><span class="s1">For painter Mi
 chael Berryhill\, there's no difference between realism and abstractio
 n. His work reminds the viewer of the challenge of capturing the process o
 f painting\, and the physical and conceptual layering that a surface might
  contain.</span></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1">Berryhill has had sol
 o exhibitions at Night Gallery in Los Angeles and at both Kate Werble an
 d Derek Eller galleries in New York City and been reviewed in The New York
  Times\, Hyperallergic\, Art in America\, Artforum\, The Brooklyn Rail\, M
 odern Painters\, Huffington Post\, Time Out NY\, Artnet News\, Flaunt maga
 zine\, Whitehot Magazine of Contemporary Art\, L Magazine\, and artcri
 tical.</span></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1">Berryhill earned his M.F.A
 . from Columbia University and has held visiting faculty positions at Bard
 \, Columbia\, Pratt\, and VCU. Berryhill was Dean of Skowhegan School of
  Painting and Sculpture for two years. He was artist-in-residence at the U
 niversity of Tennessee\, Knoxville and Virginia Commonwealth University in
  Richmond\, Virginia and held the Painting's Edge Residency at Idyllwild A
 rts Academy in California. He received a New York Foundation for the Arts 
 Fellowship for Painting and was a Studio Space recipient at the Marie Wa
 lsh Sharpe Art Foundation.</span></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1">Born i
 n El Paso\, Texas\, Michael Berryhill earned his undergraduate degree at
  University of Texas Austin. He lives and works in Ellenville\, New York.<
 /span></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1"><strong>Artist's instagram:</stro
 ng>  @berryhillmichael </span></p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<div>\n  Yaël Ksander\n</div>\n<div>\n  Director
  of Communications and Marketing\n</div>\n<div>\n  Eskenazi School of Art\
 , Architecture + Design\n</div>\n<div>\n  <a href="mailto:yksander@iu.edu"
 >yksander@iu.edu</a>\n</div>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2405020
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/11/width/168/height
 /168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,768\,768/32328_Michael-Berryhill-portrait-in-
 studio-CROPPED-WEB.rev.1788367315.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:Michael Berryhill
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>The McKinney Visiting Artist series presents a talk
  by Michael Berryhill\, who creates enigmatic paintings that arise from dr
 awings and allude to subjects\, often human or animal figures.</p>
