X-SOURCE-ID:browncounty
SUMMARY:Amplify Nashville featuring The Reverend Peyton’s Big Damn Band 
 Amplify Nashville featuring The Reverend Peyton’s Big Damn Band
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261108T003000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261108T003000
DTSTAMP:20260430T145538Z
UID:MEC-e38386b3d1dc2290eeb97ddd95f3715e@browncounty.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261108T003000
SEQUENCE:4
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 06/2-scaled.jpeg
CATEGORIES:Entertainment,Festivals,Food &amp\; Drink,Happening,Live Music
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260430
DESCRIPTION:A unique community showcase celebrating local and regional tal
 ent rooted in South Central Indiana and the surrounding areas\, Amplify Na
 shville returns to the Brown County Music Center in Nashville\, Ind.\, on 
 Saturday\, November 7\, 2026. Presented by the Brown County Music Associat
 ion\, this evening brings rising artists to the biggest stage in town\, wh
 ere they can share the spotlight with one of the area’s most celebrated 
 nationally touring acts: The Reverend Peyton’s Big Damn Band.\nThe eveni
 ng opens with Sami Riggs\, the fan-selected winner of the 2025 Brown Count
 y Songwriter Showdown. From there\, the spotlight turns to two outstanding
  bands chosen through the inaugural Rumble on the Rocks competition at Har
 d Truth Distilling on May 30\, June 6\, and June 13. These emerging artist
 s will be selected through a combination of fan votes and judges’ scores
 .\nHeadlining the night is Brown County’s own: The Reverend Peyton’s B
 ig Damn Band\, often called “the greatest front-porch blues band in the 
 world.” Led by master finger-picker Reverend Peyton\, the trio—featuri
 ng washboard virtuoso Breezy Peyton and drummer Jacob “The Snakob” Pow
 ell—has carried their electrifying country-blues sound to 38 countries a
 nd 48 states. With No. 1 records on the Billboard Blues Chart and acclaim 
 from Rolling Stone and others\, their music is rooted in heart\, tradition
 \, and a live show that leaves audiences clapping\, stomping\, and singing
  along.\nAt Amplify Nashville\, every ticket helps make a difference. Proc
 eeds from the event support Nashville area food pantry Mother’s Cupboard
  and other Nashville-area charities\, helping strengthen the community tha
 t inspires the music.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260630
LOCATION:200 Maple Leaf Boulevard\, Nashville\, IN 47448
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
