DESCRIPTION:If you've always felt like you didn't know how to look at art\
 , you've come to the right place\; bring your lunch and hop on Zoom as we 
 show you a tried-and-true method for looking at things.  On the second Mon
 day of each month\, join Eskenazi Museum of Art's resident Arts-based Well
 ness Experiences Manager Keaton Evans-Black to look at and talk about a pi
 ece of art from the IU museum collections using the see\, think\, wonder f
 ramework.  No previous art experience necessary!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260423T161734Z
LOCATION:Virtual
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2274787-virtual-event-how-to-view-ar
 t
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  If you've always felt like you didn't kn
 ow how to look at art\, you've come to the right place\; bring your lunch 
 and hop on Zoom as we show you a tried-and-true method for looking at thin
 gs.</p><p>  On the second Monday of each month\, join Eskenazi Museum of A
 rt's resident Arts-based Wellness Experiences Manager Keaton Evans-Black t
 o look at and talk about a piece of art from the IU museum collections usi
 ng the see\, think\, wonder framework.</p><p>  No previous art experience 
 necessary!</p>
