X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Eskenazi School of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2154835-tattoo-design-workshop", "Architecture + Design": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2154835-tattoo-design-workshop", "IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2298123-tattoo-design-workshop", "Eskenazi Museum of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2298123-tattoo-design-workshop"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 11": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2154835-tattoo-design-workshop"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:Tattoo Design Workshop
DTSTART:20261110T190000Z
DTEND:20261110T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20260105T151232Z
UID:20260908T190000Z-2298133@events.iu.edu__20261110
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1570,1600/24478_xx71.14.11_o3.rev.1732197268.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Culture and languages,Health and wel
 lness
DESCRIPTION:Have you always wanted to design your own tattoos\, but never 
 known where to find inspiration? Start at the museum!  This monthly worksh
 op provides instructions for examining art to find personal meaning inside
  it\, and how to use that meaning to design tattoos based on your own life
 ! Supplies will be provided to design tattoos. Occasional guests from the 
 local tattooing community may be featured to answer questions about tattoo
  design\, tattoo processes\, or the fascinating history of tattoos.  This 
 group meets on the 2nd Tuesday of every month\, excluding holidays and mus
 eum closures. The group will meet in the Roehm Family Art-making Studio\, 
 located inside the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the Es
 kenazi Museum of Art.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260826T142543Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2154835-tattoo-design-workshop
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Have you always wanted to design your ow
 n tattoos\, but never known where to find inspiration? Start at the museum
 !</p><p>  This monthly workshop provides instructions for examining art to
  find personal meaning inside it\, and how to use that meaning to design t
 attoos based on your own life! Supplies will be provided to design tattoos
 . Occasional guests from the local tattooing community may be featured to 
 answer questions about tattoo design\, tattoo processes\, or the fascinati
 ng history of tattoos.</p><p>  This group meets on the 2nd Tuesday of ever
 y month\, excluding holidays and museum closures. The group will meet in t
 he Roehm Family Art-making Studio\, located inside the Simpson Center for 
 Education on the 2nd floor of the Eskenazi Museum of Art.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<div>\n  <strong>Keaton Evans-Black\, LMHC\, ATR<
 /strong>\n</div>\n<div>\n  <i>Arts-Based Wellness Experiences Manager</i>\
 n</div>\n<div>\n  Sidney and Lois Eskenazi Museum of Art\n</div>\n<div>\n 
  Indiana University\n</div>\n<div>\n  kevansbl@iu.edu\, (812) 855-5942\n</
 div>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
