DESCRIPTION:Students will look closely at still life paintings in the gall
 eries\, discovering how artists use symbolism and lighting to communicate 
 mood and reveal more than meets the eye. After finding inspiration in the 
 galleries\, students will create their own still life paintings by arrangi
 ng and observing objects at their table to tell their own unique stories! 
  Program designed by our licensed art educator for students in grades K-12
 .Know Before You Go:  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2
 nd floor of the museum at 10 am. Together\, we'll drop off personal items 
 before exploring the galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire ou
 r project\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to creat
 e our own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!  Strollers are w
 elcome. Chaperone required. We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with o
 ne adult for every 6 children.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260716T161528Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344749-homeschool-day-tabletop-trea
 sures-am-session
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Students will look closely at still life
  paintings in the galleries\, discovering how artists use symbolism and li
 ghting to communicate mood and reveal more than meets the eye. After findi
 ng inspiration in the galleries\, students will create their own still lif
 e paintings by arranging and observing objects at their table to tell thei
 r own unique stories!</p><p>  Program designed by our licensed art educato
 r for students in grades K-12.</p><p><strong>Know Before You Go:</strong><
 /p><p>  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of th
 e museum at 10 am. Together\, we'll drop off personal items before explori
 ng the galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we
 'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own mast
 erpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!</p><p>  Strollers are welcome.
  <strong>Chaperone required.</strong> We ask that chaperones be 18 or olde
 r\, with one adult for every 6 children.</p>
