DESCRIPTION:Outfitting IU Athletics: Hoosier Champions                  Th
 is exhibit showcases objects from IU's championship teams and athletes\, c
 onnecting them to historic achievements in the Big Ten and the national st
 age. The items featured in the exhibit are from the IU Athletics Sports Me
 morabilia Collection and feature photos and videos provided by IU Athletic
 s and Indiana University Archives.                Dates: November 14\, 202
 5 - October 2026          &#160\;                  &#160\;        By Their
  Own Hands: The Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame!          Founded in 1974 by
  the Culture and Ethnic Affairs Guild of the Oakland Museum of California\
 , the Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame began as a film lecture series and awa
 rds ceremony celebrating achievements of Black film industry figures. When
  that organization closed\, they donated their materials to IU. In collabo
 ration with the IU Black Film Center and Archive\, this exhibit features o
 bjects from that collection\, including founding documents\, costumes\, an
 d handprints of inductees to the Hall of Fame.        Dates: September 202
 5 - December 2026          &#160\;                  &#160\;        Capturi
 ng the Campus: T.C. Steele\, Indiana University's First Artist in Residenc
 eCapturing the Campus pays tribute to renowned Hoosier artist T.C. Steele.
  The exhibit honors the century that has passed since his death by showcas
 ing paintings form the artist's residency at IU and other relevant works. 
 The exhibit will bring together Steele's landscapes from the IU Public Art
  and Cultural Heritage Collection and the Indiana State Museum and Histori
 c Sites' collection\, allowing the holdings of these two collections to be
  viewed in one space.        Dates: April 17\, 2026 - April 2026          
 &#160\;        Multipurpose Room          Currently Featuring: The Gift of
  Collecting: Tina Jernigan          Jernigan was a passionate supporter of
  both Indiana University and the arts. She donated artworks to the IU Publ
 ic Art and Cultural Heritage Collection upon her passing in 2024. With fun
 ding provided by Jernigan\, Public Art professionally framed\, hung\, and 
 preserved these pieces for this exhibit in the McCalla Building and for fu
 ture installations on campus.&#160\;        Dates: July 2026-July 2027&#16
 0\;  &#160\;  &#160\;  &#160\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T142940Z
LOCATION:McCalla Center\, 525 E. 9th Street\, Bloomington\, Indiana 47408
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2338209-mccalla-open-gallery-hours
