X-SOURCE:IU Jacobs School of Music
DTSTART:20261203T003000Z
DTEND:20261203T023000Z
LOCATION:Auer Hall
SUMMARY:Baroque Orchestra – Ingrid Matthews\, director
DESCRIPTION:Repertoire to be announcedAbout the DirectorIngrid Matthews i
 s professor of practice in historical performance (baroque violin) at the
  Indiana University Jacobs School of Music. A graduate of IU\, where she 
 studied with Josef Gingold and Stanley Ritchie\, Matthews is one of today
 's most respected baroque violinists. Since winning first prize in the Er
 win Bodky International Competition for Early Music in 1989\, she has app
 eared as soloist\, guest director\, chamber musician\, and concertmaster 
 with leading early music ensembles\, including the New York Collegium\, A
 ustralian Brandenburg Orchestra\, Boston Early Music Festival Orchestra\,
  Ars Lyrica (Houston)\, Tafelmusik Baroque Orchestra (Toronto)\, Musica P
 acifica (San Francisco)\, and many others. Matthews cofounded the Seattle
  Baroque Orchestra in 1994 and served as its music director until 2013. M
 atthews has won high critical acclaim for her extensive discography. Her 
 recording J. S. Bach: Complete Sonatas and Partitas for Violin was named 
 "top recommendation for this music . . . on either period or modern instr
 uments" by American Record Guide. She also plays jazz and swing styles an
 d is active as a visual artist.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><em>Repertoire to be announced</em><br />
 <br /><strong>About the Director</strong><br /><br /><strong>Ingrid Matth
 ews</strong> is professor of practice in historical performance (baroque 
 violin) at the Indiana University Jacobs School of Music. A graduate of I
 U\, where she studied with Josef Gingold and Stanley Ritchie\, Matthews i
 s one of today's most respected baroque violinists. Since winning first p
 rize in the Erwin Bodky International Competition for Early Music in 1989
 \, she has appeared as soloist\, guest director\, chamber musician\, and 
 concertmaster with leading early music ensembles\, including the New York
  Collegium\, Australian Brandenburg Orchestra\, Boston Early Music Festiv
 al Orchestra\, Ars Lyrica (Houston)\, Tafelmusik Baroque Orchestra (Toron
 to)\, Musica Pacifica (San Francisco)\, and many others. Matthews cofound
 ed the Seattle Baroque Orchestra in 1994 and served as its music director
  until 2013. Matthews has won high critical acclaim for her extensive dis
 cography. Her recording <em>J. S. Bach: Complete Sonatas and Partitas for
  Violin</em> was named "top recommendation for this music . . . on either
  period or modern instruments" by <em>American Record Guide</em>. She als
 o plays jazz and swing styles and is active as a visual artist.</p>
UID:20261203T003000Z-2387891@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260820T102247Z
