 /><br />  Bass-baritone and composer <strong>Robert Samels</strong> was b
 orn on June 2\, 1981\, and died in a plane crash on April 20\, 2006. He w
 as a doctoral student in choral conducting at the Indiana University Jaco
 bs School of Music and had studied voice with Giorgio Tozzi and Costanza 
 Cuccaro. He began his vocal studies with Alfred Anderson at the Universit
 y of Akron and Andreas Poulimenos at Bowling Green State University. Same
 ls had recently appeared as Mr. Gibbs in the world premiere of <em>Our To
 wn</em> by Ned Rorem\, as Marco in the collegiate premiere of William Bol
